\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen's rebound soothes, but still wary. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,039 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2001\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  clawed back \par \par \uc2  some gains late on Friday on the back of the yen's rebound \par \par \uc2  ahead of the weekend and New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2      Financial markets in Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, \par \par \uc2  Philippines and Thailand will be closed on New Year's eve while \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Taiwan and Korea will operate on Monday. \par \par \uc2      Trading sessions will be shortened in Singapore. Otherwise, \par \par \uc2  most Asian markets will reopen on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2      The yen rebounded to a session high of around 130.75 after \par \par \uc2  the dollar dipped in a bout of dollar profit-taking and \par \par \uc2  option-related sales. \par \par \uc2      By late Tokyo trade, the yen fell again around 131.50 on \par \par \uc2  expectations the Japanese officials would continue to show no \par \par \uc2  sign of tempering their apparent acceptance of a lower yen. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar that touched 11-1/2-year lows at \par \par \uc2  1.8550 early on, bounced back above the 1.8500 level while the \par \par \uc2  Korean won and Taiwan dollar rose above their late Thursday \par \par \uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  But analysts expected the yen's reprieve to be short-lived. \par \par \uc2  "Moves in the dollar/yen can be vicious at times, and then \par \par \uc2  it is the year end. So most players opted to clear old \par \par \uc2  positions, square out and lock in profits while they can," a \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at a Singapore bank said. \par \par \uc2  "But the weak yen story isn't over yet. This retracement is \par \par \uc2  likely to draw in more hedging by corporates and speculators \par \par \uc2  and we'll see more weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  A weaker yen tends to raise competitiveness concerns in \par \par \uc2  Asian regional economies, with Korea, Taiwan and Singapore seen \par \par \uc2  more vulnerable given the similarity of their exports and \par \par \uc2  markets with those of Japan. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar struggled to reach higher ground but \par \par \uc2  was pulled below 1.8500 again by U.S. dollar demand from \par \par \uc2  interbank players who anticipated a weaker yen and bleak \par \par \uc2  economic data next week. \par \par \uc2  The government is scheduled to release its preliminary \par \par \uc2  fourth-quarter GDP data and the whole year's growth estimate on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast that the economy this \par \par \uc2  year will contract 2.5 percent year-on-year but grow 1.7 \par \par \uc2  percent in 2002. \par \par \uc2  Charts show the U.S. dollar remains heavily overbought \par \par \uc2  against the Sing dollar on the 14-day relative strength index, \par \par \uc2  indicating further correction ahead. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht eked out some gains on last-minute exporter dollar \par \par \uc2  offers, with a minor rebound in the yen providing some support. \par \par \uc2  The market was near to holiday mood and paid little \par \par \uc2  attention to the economic data released by the Bank of Thailand \par \par \uc2  on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In November, exports contracted 12.8 percent on the year \par \par \uc2  compared with a year-on-year decline of 14.3 percent while \par \par \uc2  imports shrank 8.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  Despite a drop in trade surplus, the country's current \par \par \uc2  account surplus rose to $537 million from $531 million in \par \par \uc2  October. \par \par \uc2  Further gains in the dollar could be dented by rising baht \par \par \uc2  funding costs in the offshore market, with the one-month rate \par \par \uc2  now quoted at 18/26 satang per dollar against 16/28 late on \par \par \uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar regained lost ground and closed higher \par \par \uc2  after 11 straight sessions of decline, drawing strength from \par \par \uc2  the yen's rebound. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 35.084 to the dollar on Friday after \par \par \uc2  finishing at a 15-year closing low of 35.127 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said players trimmed their long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions while there were no signs of the usually active \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on either side of the market. \par \par \uc2      The market ranged between an intraday low of 35.186 and a \par \par \uc2  high of 35.051. The Taiwan dollar's weakest level this year was \par \par \uc2  an intraday trough of 35.30 in July. \par \par \uc2      Charts showed the dollar was still overbought, with the \par \par \uc2  14-day relative strength index reading at 84.171, but was much \par \par \uc2  lower than 99.183 level seen earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso ended onshore trade lower but was off its early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trough as players covered short peso positions ahead of a long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Monday and Tuesday will be public holidays in Manila and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets will resume trading on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said importers and corporates pushed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar higher earlier but later took a cue from the yen and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par squared out of those positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said she was satisfied\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the level of the peso even if it did not strengthen to 50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as she had previously hoped. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at around 53.61\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the dollar when Arroyo set the target earlier this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah slipped to a low of 10,480 before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports-related inflows pushed it back to around 10,350.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said the rupiah was under pressure in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early trade from a pick-up in commercial dollar demand, but the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volumes were not large enough to have a big impact on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said corporates had remained cautious\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in recent sessions due to dollar sales by exporters for their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-end requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money market, Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates unchanged at 15.125 percent for the overnight rate and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 15.875 percent for the seven-day rate.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     131.23       131.64         +0.31\par  Sing dlr      1.8518       1.8496         -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    35.084       35.127         +0.12\par  Korean won   1320.00      1308.00         -0.91\par  Baht           44.19        44.20         +0.02\par  Peso           51.60        51.49         -0.21\par  Rupiah      10388.00     10365.00         -0.22\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     131.23       114.45        -12.79\par  Sing dlr      1.8518       1.7365         -6.23\par  Taiwan dlr    35.084       32.900         -6.23\par  Korean won   1320.00      1277.00         -3.26\par  Baht           44.19        43.70         -1.11\par  Peso           51.60        50.75         -1.65\par  Rupiah      10388.00      9470.00         -8.84\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011228dxcs00kde\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
