\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Defiant to yen weakness, inflows watched. \b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2001\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  refused to \par \par \uc2  buckle under the yen's weakness in early trade on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, drawing support from seasonal capital inflows and \par \par \uc2  demand for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dealers said foreign investors, loathe to report too much \par \par \uc2  cash at the year's end, have been dumping funds into stocks. \par \par \uc2      Dollar offers from exporters and banks seeking to trim long \par \par \uc2  dollar positions ahead of the year end also supported regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The yen sank to a new eight-month low of 126.58 against the \par \par \uc2  dollar overnight on a report by hedge fund group Medley Global \par \par \uc2  Advisory quoting a U.S. official as saying there was no lower \par \par \uc2  limit on the Japanese unit. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  clawed back some gains after the Treasury \par \par \uc2  Department said the report did not reflect the agency's \par \par \uc2  position. \par \par \uc2  The market will be watching closely the U.S. November \par \par \uc2  retail sales report due later in the day. It will shed light on \par \par \uc2  consumer spending which accounts for two-thirds of economic \par \par \uc2  activity. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Gains in some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the Thai baht \par \par \uc2  and the Indonesian rupiah, provided some psychological support \par \par \uc2  for the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared some of its earlier gains after the \par \par \uc2  yen sank back below 126 to the dollar as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  carries substantial weight in Singapore's trade-weighted basket \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected market participants to sell the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar on its way to 1.8350 - the level seen as a near-term \par \par \uc2  support for the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht ran into some resistance at around 43.65 where \par \par \uc2  some players started picking up dollars again, but sporadic \par \par \uc2  dollar sales by exporters and offshore players helped underpin \par \par \uc2  the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Charts show the baht well-supported at 44.10, the \par \par \uc2  38.2-percent retracement of the dollar/baht's October \par \par \uc2  25-December 13 downmove. \par \par \uc2  The market is divided over the direction of Thai interest \par \par \uc2  rates. Some analysts were betting the Bank of Thailand would \par \par \uc2  deliver a long overdue rate cut at its next policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  But others argued there was no point for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to cut rates unless the U.S. economy deteriorated further to \par \par \uc2  the point that it was necessary for the Fed to extend its \par \par \uc2  easing cycle. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won managed to defy the yen's gravitational pull and \par \par \uc2  opened slightly higher at 1,272.50, compared with the \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's close of 1,274.4. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was well-supported by expectations of \par \par \uc2  heavy foreign direct investments, but its upside was dented a \par \par \uc2  bit by the yen's weakness and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Jin Nyum said his ministry was well aware \par \par \uc2  of negative impact of the yen's weakness on the Korean economy \par \par \uc2  and was closely watching its movement. \par \par \uc2  Market sources estimated that December FDI could exceed \par \par \uc2  $2.0 billion. This includes 244 billion won (US$191.5 million) \par \par \uc2  to LG Group's energy units and 155 billion won (US$121.7 \par \par \uc2  million) to Shinhan Finance Holding Co . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was hovering around 10,000 due to recent \par \par \uc2  dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Gains were \par \par \uc2  exaggerated by paper-thin trading volumes ahead of the Muslim \par \par \uc2  Eid al-Fitr holiday which marks the end of the fasting month. \par \par \uc2      Corporate players also slowed down buying the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  ahead of the year-end. \par \par \uc2      On the macro front, Bank Indonesia said on Wednesday it \par \par \uc2  expected the economy to grow by up to 3.6 percent in the fourth \par \par \uc2  quarter and up to four percent for the full year, but some \par \par \uc2  analysts said these figures were overly optimistic. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecasts were roughly in line with \par \par \uc2  earlier official figures, but much lower than the 4.77 percent \par \par \uc2  growth recorded last year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     126.04       125.92         -0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.8295       1.8293         -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.458       34.455         -0.01\par  Korean won   1264.40      1268.30         +0.31\par  Baht           43.70        43.73         +0.07\par  Peso           51.98        51.98         +0.00\par  Rupiah       9985.00     10000.00         +0.15\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     126.04       114.45         -9.20\par  Sing dlr      1.8295       1.7365         -5.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.458       32.900         -4.52\par  Korean won   1264.40      1277.00         +1.00\par  Baht           43.70        43.70         +0.00\par  Peso           51.98        50.75         -2.37\par  Rupiah       9985.00      9470.00         -5.16\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011213dxcd0066e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
