\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Hold on but eye wobbly yen, Fed meeting. \b0\par\par\uc2 983 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2001\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Dec 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held their \par \par \uc2  ground late Tuesday helped by a lack of trading interest in \par \par \uc2  face of a wobbly yen , the Federal Reserve's rate \par \par \uc2  decision and  the approaching holiday season. \par \par \uc2      The dollar gave up its overnight eight-month peaks against \par \par \uc2  the yen, but mounting gloom about the state of the Japanese \par \par \uc2  economy kept it supported. \par \par \uc2      But the yen has been of lesser concern to regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of late, with equity-related inflows and rising \par \par \uc2  optimism on a rebound in the U.S. economy, their major export \par \par \uc2  market, instilling some resilience. \par \par \uc2      Though Wall Street's recent losses wiped out part of last \par \par \uc2  week's equity gains across the region, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players choose \par \par \uc2  to stick to their positions ahead of the Fed's widely expected \par \par \uc2  25 basis point cut in its 2.0 percent fund rate later Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      In local events, Bangkok offered foreign companies tax \par \par \uc2  breaks to set up their regional offices in Thailand as part of \par \par \uc2  an incentive package to attract foreign investment. \par \par \uc2      Korea's import and export prices for November showed a \par \par \uc2  declined from October, suggesting easing demand both at home \par \par \uc2  and abroad. \par \par \uc2      And industrial output in China rose 7.9 percent in \par \par \uc2  November, its lowest in nearly two years, indicating the impact \par \par \uc2  on the broader economy from the global downturn. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won edged up as settlement of local stocks bought by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors last week resulted in some inflows in the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said news that Korea Telecom plans to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell up to 15 percent of its stake to foreign investors,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including five percent new shares supported the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That dealers said countered to some extent the impact of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent net sale of local stocks by foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the upside was seen capped by worries that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations of a steep fall in the yen could prompt players to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cover their short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was steady at the close of onshore trade as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates kept to the sidelines, while year-end inflows and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remittances from overseas workers capped the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, dealers said peso stability was more due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctance to trade ahead of the expected Fed rate cut which is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to be followed by a cut of its own by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Media reports have estimated dollar remittances by overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Filipino workers, which traditionally accelerate in the last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter, were expected to be down by at least $600 million this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year from last year's $6.05 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht strode higher on the back of dollar offers from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters and some U.S. names in the offshore market who had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overhedged their positions earlier this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore and Bangkok said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was also underpinned by expectations of wider interest rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par differentials.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the market is speculating that the U.S. Federal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserve will slash key interest rates at its meeting on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday, it reckons the Bank of Thailand will not follow suit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht funding costs in the offshore market rose slightly to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10/15 satang to the dollar for the one-month rate and 150/171\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par satang for the 12-month rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended barely changed at 34.455 after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading in a tight range of 34.448-34.461, with minimal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was weighed down by losses in the local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, with foreign investors being net sellers of T$714\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion (US$20.7 million) in domestic shares on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market was subdued as players took a wait-and-see\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stance ahead of the Fed's meeting later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah broke past the 10,200 level for the first time\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since October 25 thanks to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and fewer dollar bids from local corporates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said trading activity was getting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lighter ahead of the Eid-Al-Fitr holiday this weekend, and most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates had fulfilled their dollar requirements ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nevertheless, players hesitated from driving the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par much higher given Indonesia's tricky economic fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the market shrugged off news that the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to complete this year its merger process for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar spent the session not far from its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opening levels of around 1.83.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar/Sing found itself confined in a tight range of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8293-1.8321. The market struggled first to break the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bottom-side, but ran into the dollar bids. It later tried to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par test the upside, only to run into dollar profit-taking.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market was looking for direction, knowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the weaker yen and the city-state's poor fundamentals were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capping the Sing dollar's upside. However, a stronger euro and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the more confident tone among the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from sliding too far.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  AT 0821 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     126.05       125.92         -0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.8319       1.8336         +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.456       34.457         +0.00\par  Korean won   1272.60      1280.00         +0.58\par  Baht           43.76        43.91         +0.34\par  Peso           51.95        51.90         -0.09\par  Rupiah      10230.00     10230.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     126.05       114.45         -9.20\par  Sing dlr      1.8319       1.7365         -5.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.456       32.900         -4.52\par  Korean won   1272.60      1277.00         +0.35\par  Baht           43.76        43.70         -0.14\par  Peso           51.95        50.75         -2.30\par  Rupiah      10230.00      9470.00         -7.43\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011211dxcb00m3j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
