\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Higher As State Bks On Sidelines \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2001\par 10:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Thursday as large state-owned banks, which in recent weeks have been buying dollars for customers, remained out of the market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  State-owned Bank Mandiri and other banks were sidelined, which took the pressure off the rupiah. Indonesian companies need to repay dollar debts by the year-end, which has hurt the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the debt repayment flow may now be easing. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also rumored to be active Thursday selling dollars, although there was no confirmation of this from the bank itself. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah but never comments on individual actions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at IDR10,425, down from IDR10,470 at Wednesday's finish. \par \par \uc2  But it's still unclear whether debt repayments from companies will stay at lower levels for the remainder of this year. Few banks have a clear idea of exactly what amount of debt companies still have to repay. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved to an intraday high of IDR10,475 Thursday as players continued to buy the U.S. unit on the belief that Bank Mandiri would be active buying on behalf of corporate clients - mainly state-owned companies. But this buying didn't materialize. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah should remain in a tight range against the dollar for the rest of the year. The dollar remains strongly supported at IDR10,300 due to continued concerns over the country's debt situation. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wrightdowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011206dxc600k9c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
