\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Directionless, local factors rule. \b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2001\par 11:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed \par \par \uc2  bag in late trade on Wednesday as investors looked to local \par \par \uc2  factors for clues on direction. \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht repeatedly failed to break above the key \par \par \uc2  barrier of 44.00 to the dollar amid rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  was in the market to tame its recent rapid rise. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won was dragged down by losses in the local \par \par \uc2  stock market, but it was lifted from its intraday trough by \par \par \uc2  dollar sales by exporters. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, the yen clawed back some gains against both the \par \par \uc2  dollar and the euro despite Standard & Poor's downgrading \par \par \uc2  Japan's sovereign rating by a single notch to AA. \par \par \uc2      However, dealers said the single-notch downgrade was better \par \par \uc2  than the two notches many had feared. \par \par \uc2      Going forward, the market will be watching data on U.S. \par \par \uc2  jobless claims due out on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Thailand will release its monthly economic data \par \par \uc2  on Friday, which include trade and current account balances and \par \par \uc2  manufacturing production. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar found some consolation in the steadier \par \par \uc2  yen, but was thwarted in its attempts to rise by players still \par \par \uc2  bearish over the city-state's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2      Analysts say the Sing dollar has struggled to gain any \par \par \uc2  ground because of the market's view that Singapore still needs \par \par \uc2  to stick to an easy monetary policy to see it through the bad \par \par \uc2  economic times. \par \par \uc2  Unlike other countries, Singapore uses its trade-weighted \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar as its main monetary policy tool rather than \par \par \uc2  interest rates. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the prevailing market philosophy was to buy \par \par \uc2  dollar on dips, unless the dollar/yen falls past 123.50. \par \par \uc2      KOREAN WON 2 \par \par \uc2      The won finished sharply lower against the U.S. dollar due \par \par \uc2  to hefty losses in local stocks and growing fears of a \par \par \uc2  potential war between the United States and Iraq. \par \par \uc2      The won ended at 1,272.1 per dollar against Tuesday's close \par \par \uc2  of 1,265.30. Foreign investors were net sellers of 15 billion \par \par \uc2  won of local stocks. \par \par \uc2      Exporter dollar sales trimmed some losses, but were not \par \par \uc2  enough to lift the won to close in positive territory. \par \par \uc2      On the data front, the October current account surplus came \par \par \uc2  in at $388 million, down from $708 million in September. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Talk of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht back from breaking above 44 again on Wednesday despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong demand for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts show 44.30 as the dollar/baht near-term resistance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht funding costs in the offshore market eased slightly,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the one-month forward rate quoted at 5/9 satang per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against 7/10 satang earlier.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah struggled to bat off the 10,500 level despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted selling around $10 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market early in the session, dealers in Jakarta said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nevertheless, state banks were quick to pick up the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shoving the rupiah to a low of 10,525.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market remained impervious to news of the government's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attempts to dispose of assets ahead of the year-end. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government said it will make a decision this week about its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plan to sell a majority stake in state-owned PT Semen Gresik to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico's Cemex. Jakarta has been trying to sell the stake for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par three years, and its plan was recently foiled by the West\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sumatran government's take-over of a Gresik unit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar maintained its poise despite losses on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indeed, foreign investors remained net buyers of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks, purchasing a net T$859.2 million in Taiwan stocks even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the benchmark TAIEX slipped by over two percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said the Taiwan dollar's decorum was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also largely due to the market's general reluctance to test the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's determination to keep the exchange rate steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of key parliamentary elections on Saturday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR #N/A DRP GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.15       124.13         +0.80\par  Sing dlr      1.8330       1.8332         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.467       34.468         +0.00\par  Korean won   1271.50      1262.50         -0.71\par  Baht           44.07        44.06         -0.02\par  Peso           51.97        52.03         +0.13\par  Rupiah      10425.00     10415.00         -0.10\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.15       114.45         -7.06\par  Sing dlr      1.8330       1.7365         -5.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.467       32.900         -4.55\par  Korean won   1271.50      1277.00         +0.43\par  Baht           44.07        43.70         -0.84\par  Peso           51.97        50.75         -2.34\par  Rupiah      10425.00      9470.00         -9.16\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011128dxbs00idj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
