\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Down As Ctrl Bk Stays On Sidelines \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2001\par 10:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended weaker Tuesday as players covered short-dollar positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Local banks had built up short-dollar positions on expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell dollars in the market to help buoy the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  This pushed the dollar to an intraday low at IDR10,320. But after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , most players began to unwind positions in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Asian trading Tuesday at IDR10,420, slightly higher than IDR10,400 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Monday, helping push the rupiah higher in thin trade. The bank has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but doesn't comment on specific actions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should find strong support Wednesday at IDR10,350, with resistance at IDR10,500. \par \par \uc2  In the longer term, Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain under pressure as investors are concerned over the country's huge levels of foreign debt. Government foreign debt alone is about $70 billion. \par \par \uc2  Repayment of debt for the rest of this year is likely to keep the lid on any rupiah gains, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; tom.wrightdowjones.com 