\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Slightly hung over from recent rises. \b0\par\par\uc2 980 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2001\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave \par \par \uc2  up \par \par \uc2   ground late on Tuesday, wobbling slightly after their recent \par \par \uc2  dizzying rises. \par \par \uc2      As with recent sessions, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seeing the most capital \par \par \uc2  inflows into local asset markets fared better during the \par \par \uc2  session. Still, the Korean won, which had led the charge \par \par \uc2  against the dollar, was slightly deflated after the benchmark \par \par \uc2  Korea Composite Stock Price Index ended a touch lower. \par \par \uc2      All in all, though, the yen's nervous state did not have \par \par \uc2  much of an impact on the cheerful tone of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  with the exception of the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were benefiting from \par \par \uc2  rising hopes in local markets over the possibility of a U.S. \par \par \uc2  recovery in the second half of next year, which would pull Asia \par \par \uc2  out of its economic doldrums. \par \par \uc2      Some analysts were slightly puzzled as to how regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to ignore the yen and focus purely on \par \par \uc2  the U.S. recovery hopes given the fact that Japan is still the \par \par \uc2  region's largest economy. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht continued to defy the yen, itching to break above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44 to the dollar on exporter dollar offers and dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Singapore names.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite strong inflows coming into Thailand recently, the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decided on Tuesday to keep its benchmark 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repo rate unchanged at 2.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Assistant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Bandid Nijathaworn told a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news conference the ratio of Thailand's foreign reserves to its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term debt was at a healthy level of 138 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was ready to ease monetary policy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if the country's economic outlook worsened.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Baht funding costs were mostly steady, with the one-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forward rate quoted at 7/9 satang per dollar and the 12-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate at 125/135 satang.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won softened slightly after local stocks took a dip and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean authorities continued to wag their fingers in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disapproval at the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With the yen and won cross rate nearing lows not seen since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par October 2000 according to Reuters data, officials in Seoul\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stepped up their campaign in maintaining Korea's export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness. An official from the finance minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par threatened action if the won continued to rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, a foreign bank dealer in Singapore said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities were more likely looking to smooth the won's rise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rather than prevent it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors continued to be net buyers of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks, purchasing 65 billion won of Korean shares on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar shuffled around the 1.8350/60 level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with players still tuning into the yen's travails rather than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the firmness in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     To the Sing dollar's relief, however, dealers described the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market as being exhausted, with few having the energy to push\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar/Sing higher. A U.S. bank dealer said there was good\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-way interest in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That said, if dollar/yen moves much higher overnight, there\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could be more losses in store for the Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Unlike its regional counterparts, the Sing dollar has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beholden to the yen given the fact that it is managed according\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to its trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in which the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has a large weighting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts also add the Sing dollar has not enjoyed the kind\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of inflows Korea and Taiwan have in recent weeks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local corporate demand for the dollar drove the peso below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 52 in a market unnerved by the fighting in the southern\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Government troops and Muslim gunmen loyal to a rebellious\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par governor continued their battle on the outskirts of the city of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Zamboanga, leaving at least 28 people dead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the violence coupled with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's sagging economy drove the peso lower with corporate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar bids emerging on any dips below the 52 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A local bank dealer in Manila said power and oil firms have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been strong buyers of the dollar recently.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was wedged in a narrow range, underpinned by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  invention and receding dollar demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said one-state oil firm remained a major buyer of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the calm market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the fiscal front, Indonesia posted a 16.5 trillion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah ($1.6 billion) budget deficit for the first 10 months,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but most analysts forecast it will not deepen beyond the yearly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par target of 54.3 trillion rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rupiah interbank money market unchanged at 15.125 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for the overnight rate and 15.875 percent for the seven-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar continued to advance against the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar despite some consolidation in the local stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was boosted by seasonal exporter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales and improved earnings outlook for some major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par semiconductor companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar closed at 34.468 to the dollar compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with 34.465 at the open and 34.480 at the close on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.33       124.07         -0.21\par  Sing dlr      1.8356       1.8304         -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr    34.468       34.480         +0.03\par  Korean won   1262.50      1262.00         -0.04\par  Baht           44.07        44.16         +0.20\par  Peso           52.03        51.89         -0.27\par  Rupiah      10410.00     10320.00         -0.86\par  Ringgit       3.7995       1.7995        -52.64\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.33       114.45         -7.95\par  Sing dlr      1.8356       1.7365         -5.40\par  Taiwan dlr    34.468       32.900         -4.55\par  Korean won   1262.50      1277.00         +1.15\par  Baht           44.07        43.70         -0.84\par  Peso           52.03        50.75         -2.46\par  Rupiah      10410.00      9470.00         -9.03\par  Ringgi