\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Charge higher, but c.banks stand in way. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,026 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2001\par 10:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 26 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reclaimed \par \par \uc2  lost ground against the dollar late on Monday, propped up by \par \par \uc2  capital inflows in local asset markets. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won led the charge against the dollar, touching \par \par \uc2  seven-month highs despite verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Korean \par \par \uc2  authorities. Even suspected dollar sales by the authorities \par \par \uc2  failed to dampen the won's high spirits. \par \par \uc2  With foreign funds showing little sign of letting up on \par \par \uc2  their buying spree of Korean stocks, more and more analysts are \par \par \uc2  saying Korea is one of the few bright spots in Asia. \par \par \uc2  But the cheer in Korea was spilling over to other regional \par \par \uc2  markets, with the Thai baht and Taiwan dollar also recouping \par \par \uc2  some ground from the dollar thanks to news of their own capital \par \par \uc2  inflows. \par \par \uc2  While they were temporarily outnumbered, pessimists said \par \par \uc2  the strength in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to last in the \par \par \uc2  long term, especially in view of the weaker yen. They say the \par \par \uc2  recent strength in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also largely due to \par \par \uc2  the excessive long dollar positions being held in the regional \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts say if weakness in the yen persists, central \par \par \uc2  banks were more likely to step up their efforts to prevent \par \par \uc2  their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising too much to protect their export \par \par \uc2  competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won stole the limelight, rising to levels not seen \par \par \uc2  since March this year on soaring sentiment. \par \par \uc2  Foreign equity inflows and the country's respectable \par \par \uc2  economic performance in the face of the global economic \par \par \uc2  slowdown have helped the won rise steadily in recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index \par \par \uc2  gained 4.55 percent to close at a new 14-month high, with \par \par \uc2  foreign investors net buyers of stocks again. Since \par \par \uc2  mid-October, foreign investors have bought some $2 billion \par \par \uc2  worth of local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Korean authorities tried their best to temper the won's \par \par \uc2  rise, verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice during the day by saying the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength was not desirable given the current \par \par \uc2  economic climate. Dealers in Seoul said state banks were \par \par \uc2  spotted selling dollars in the market, but to little avail. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht touched a high of 44.07 before coming back down to \par \par \uc2  earth when foreign banks in Bangkok bought back the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Inspired by rises in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and recent \par \par \uc2  capital inflows into local markets, the baht came close to \par \par \uc2  testing 44.00 - a level it has not broken since September 17. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said the sell-off in the dollar/baht was \par \par \uc2  spurred by offshore foreign banks, who triggered a number of \par \par \uc2  stop-loss dollar sell orders. But when the baht proved unable \par \par \uc2  to reach the 44.00 level, players across the board began buying \par \par \uc2  the dollar/baht again. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said there was talk the Bank of Thailand was \par \par \uc2  on the bid for dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said in the past \par \par \uc2  that one of its priorities was to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar had a brief moment in the sun, rising \par \par \uc2  above 1.83 before dollar bulls beat it back down again. \par \par \uc2      Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to lengthen its chain to the \par \par \uc2  yen, and resisted serious falls despite the yen's wobbly state. \par \par \uc2      However, dealers said the view on the Sing dollar had not \par \par \uc2  brightened, remaining firmly negative given the city-state's \par \par \uc2  struggling economy. The government's suggestion on Friday that \par \par \uc2  Singapore's closely guarded reserves might be used to help \par \par \uc2  counteract its worst-ever recession only served to highlight \par \par \uc2  the dire straits the economy was in. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah steadied in moderate trade, with corporate \par \par \uc2  dollar bids and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar offers keeping it within a \par \par \uc2  tight range of 10,410-10.460. \par \par \uc2  After Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last \par \par \uc2  week, the market was still holding long dollar positions at the \par \par \uc2  open of trade, dealers in Jakarta said. They added dollar sales \par \par \uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Indonesian Bank Restructuring \par \par \uc2  Agency also helped the rupiah steady itself. \par \par \uc2      However, the rupiah's gains were limited because local \par \par \uc2  corporates were on the hunt for dollar. \par \par \uc2      The government continued to race against the clock in \par \par \uc2  disposing assets before the end of the year to help plug the \par \par \uc2  country's gapping budget deficit. IBRA said it has shortlisted \par \par \uc2  nine bidders for a stake of up tp 51 percent in the country's \par \par \uc2  largest retail bank, PT Bank Central Asia. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso climbed in line with the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with \par \par \uc2  a trickle of dollar inflows from overseas Filipino workers also \par \par \uc2  supporting it. \par \par \uc2  But the peso's gains were far from spectacular. Dealers in \par \par \uc2  Manila said players were unwilling to unwind their dollar \par \par \uc2  positions because the dollar inflows were largely a seasonal \par \par \uc2  factor due to Christmas. \par \par \uc2  On the bright side, elections for a new provincial governor \par \par \uc2  in the semi-autonomous Muslim region of the southern \par \par \uc2  Philippines were peaceful, despite fears of violence after a \par \par \uc2  failed revolt against Manila. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Once again, the Taiwan dollar reclaimed a bit of ground \par \par \uc2  only to cede its gains because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been keeping the \par \par \uc2  exchange rate stable amid the island's recession, was unlikely \par \par \uc2  to let go of its reins on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of key \par \par \uc2  parliamentary elections on Saturday. \par \par \uc2      Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.94       123.79         -0.12\par  Sing dlr      1.8322       1.8367         +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.480       34.481         +0.00\par  Korean won   1262.00      1271.80         +0.78\par  Baht           44.16        44.30         +0.32\par  Peso           51.89        51.99         +0.19\par  Rupiah      10380.00     10530.00         +1.45\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.94       114.45         -7.66\par  Sing dlr      1.8322       1.7365         -5.22\par  Taiwan dlr    34.480       32.900         -4.58\par  Korean won   1262.00      1277.00         +1.19\par  Baht           44.16        43.70         -1.04\par  Peso           51.89        50.75         -2.20\par  Rupiah      10380.00      9470.00         -8.77\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011126dxbq00idi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
