\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late; Renewed US Dlr Bullishness \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2001\par 11:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Friday, with the Singapore dollar feeling the brunt of the market's renewed bullishness toward the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euphoria over a slew of better-than-expected U.S. economic indicators - including a drop in jobless claims - and Wall Street's recent rally have fueled hopes that an economic rebound may be around the corner. This, combined with signs of progress in the U.S.-led military campaign against terrorism, have bolstered the dollar this week. \par \par \uc2  As speculation mounts that the U.S. Federal Reserve might reverse its current easing cycle, amid hopes the U.S. economy would recover by the second quarter of next year, the Eurodollar futures market is betting that U.S. interest rates will rise by about a percentage point next year, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "That is keeping the dollar buoyant against the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially against the Singapore dollar," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said the market is getting carried away. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they're ready to hike so quickly," said Philip Wee, a market strategist at Singapore's DBS Bank. "The market has forgotten that this is one of the worst times the Fed has had in a long while, in dealing with so many uncertainties." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was especially strong against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , climbing to S$1.8365, from S$1.8324 late Thursday, after a day of erratic trading. \par \par \uc2  A large local bank had dominated trading, selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at higher levels while picking it up again at cheaper levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As sentiment toward the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turns increasingly positive, a test of the psychologically important S$1.8400 appears imminent, market watchers said. \par \par \uc2  Even a milder-than-expected 21.6% fall in Singapore's non-oil domestic exports in October and comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore it is unlikely to ease policy further "for now" failed to ruffle the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "When we look at monetary conditions, it is currently very easy. Monetary conditions are conducive for recovery. I don't see any need for concern," said Khor Hoe Ee, a managing director at Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some market observers have been calling for the MAS to further ease monetary policy in coming months as Singapore sinks deeper into a recession. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's gross domestic product shrank 5.6% in the third quarter from a year earlier, following a 0.5% contraction in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar ended barely changed at NT$34.500 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared with NT$34.501 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated US$150 million throughout the session to offset the appreciating pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from U.S. dollar sales by exporters and foreign fund inflows, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  After the market closed, the government said Taiwan's economy contracted by 4.21% in the third quarter on-year, as the Sept. 11 attacks in the U.S. dealt a fresh blow to the already ailing global economy and demand for Taiwan's products. \par \par \uc2  The government slashed its 2001 GDP forecast to a contraction of 2.12%, from a decline of 0.37%. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar will likely show minimal reaction to the GDP data, which wasn't as bad as the market had thought; instead, persistent equity inflows will continue to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoyed, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won ended little changed, as foreign equity inflows tapered and with the yen relatively stable, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1,283.0 won, compared with KRW1,283.3 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Foreigners bought a net KRW1.1 billion in Korean shares Friday, compared with a net KRW100 billion in each of the last two sessions. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso strengthened slightly as banks, bracing for more remittance inflows from overseas Filipino workers ahead of the Christmas holidays, trimmed their long dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America said the peso also found partial support from the government's announcement earlier Friday that U.S. regulators have given the Philippines approval to sell up to US$1.2 billion in global bonds for budget support. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 51.920 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, down from PHP52.045 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dragged by the Singapore dollar, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly weaker at 44.475 baht to the U.S. dollar, compared with THB44.445 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Light \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady at IDR10,635 rupiah against the dollar, compared with IDR10,625 late Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011116dxbg000ni\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
