\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rangebound, but dollar may advance. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,006 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2001\par 02:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  stuck in recent ranges early on Wednesday, even as the dollar \par \par \uc2  held reign over the other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have recently been torn between a \par \par \uc2  softer yen and central banks keen on supporting their \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Moreover, diminishing interest in these markets \par \par \uc2  have also conspired to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hostage to their \par \par \uc2  recent ranges. \par \par \uc2      Trading in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be muted because \par \par \uc2  markets in Singapore were closed for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2      Nevertheless, any major gains by the dollar against the yen \par \par \uc2  could unnerve the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Sentiment towards the dollar received a boost after \par \par \uc2  Northern Alliance fighters in Afghanistan marched into the \par \par \uc2  capital city of Kabul as the ruling Taliban fled. That victory \par \par \uc2  in the U.S.-led campaign against the Taliban prompted players \par \par \uc2  to unwind their safe positions in the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  News, too, that a plane crash in the New York City borough \par \par \uc2  of Queens was likely an accident also becalmed a skittish \par \par \uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      Some in the market warned, however, that the euphoria may \par \par \uc2  be premature, with the U.S. economy still facing tough times. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won firmed slightly thanks to rises in the local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market. But any sign of selling by foreign investors could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reverse the won's direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Net foreign stock sales had overshadowed positive news that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard and Poor's had raised Korea's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors sold a net 68 billion won worth of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks on Tuesday after buying a net of only 11 billion won on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Korea's adjusted unemployment rate rose month-on-month in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par October to 3.5 percent from 3.3 percent in September, with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par national statistics office reporting that more people in their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thirties and fifties were seeking jobs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar held fast to its recent range of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.50 despite exporters' dollar sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been unable to muster enough strength to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par break free from the 34.50 level because of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vigilance. Dealers and analysts say the bank has been in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market nearly every day to ensure a stable exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Faced with the possibility of Taiwan's first full-year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contraction and fragile domestic confidence, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has been keen to maintain a steady rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht remained firm against the dollar, though it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par starting to look fragile as unwinding of long dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by offshore names began to slow.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A softer yen prevented the baht from gaining more ground as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign players began buying back the dollar to cover their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short dollar positions against the other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was also wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to block the baht's rise. Some in the market said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the bank was seeking to keep the baht at competitive levels,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and to balance any gains related to inflows for the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largest ever initial public offering, the sale of 30 percent of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par state oil and gas firm PTT Plc.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah steadied around above the 10,700 level, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players remaining on their toes over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But, despite the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sentiment towards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the persistently weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was glum given \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plethora of economic and political woes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the political front, the market was still skittish over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential violence after a prominent pro-independence leader in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the restive province of Irian Jaya was found dead over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend. Nearly 10,000 people turned out on Tuesday to march\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peacefully behind the body of Theys Eluay.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Underlining Indonesia's economic problems, the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chief economics minister Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti said on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday the country was not considering cutting its already\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par thin spending for the 2001 budget despite growing concerns over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's debt levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par And dealing the rupiah another blow, foreign investment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approvals in January-September fell to $6.05 billion from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $12.25 billion last year. Frightened by the country's chronic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political instability and the slow pace of reforms, foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors have been avoiding Indonesia for months, which has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par caused a dwindling supply of dollars in the market amid growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar demand from local corporates seeking to service or repay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was trapped between wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and growing fear in the market that this year's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar remittances from overseas Filipino workers was not going\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to be as strong as the market had hoped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In fact, analysts say dollar remittances were likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slow as many overseas workers may have lost their jobs because\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the global economic downturn. Some analysts argue that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par link between a stronger peso and remittances ahead of Christmas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was always tenuous.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it thought the peso may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firm to 51 to the dollar before the end of the year because of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It added that it had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for some time. But, dealers in Manila have said they suspected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that bank had been in the market to defend the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Markets in Singapore were closed because of a public\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.53       121.24         -0.24\par  Sing dlr      1.8255       1.8250         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.505       34.501         -0.01\par  Korean won   1278.00      1273.00         -0.39\par  Baht           44.45        44.42         -0.07\par  Peso           51.97        52.09         +0.23\par  Rupiah      10670.00     10670.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.53       114.45         -5.83\par  Sing dlr      1.8255       1.7365         -4.88\par  Taiwan dlr    34.505       32.900         -4.65\par  Korean won   1278.00      1277.00         -0.08\par  Baht           44.45        43.70         -1.69\par  Peso           51.97        50.75         -2.35\par  Rupiah      10670.00      9470.00        -11.25\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011114dxbe0026a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
