\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Helped by firmer yen, North Asia leads. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2001\par 03:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 9 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed \par \par \uc2  early Friday drawing strength from the yen that gained \par \par \uc2  on the back of a sharp fall in the euro . \par \par \uc2      The yen rose to one-month highs against the dollar which \par \par \uc2  was dragged down by the euro's slide to six-week lows against \par \par \uc2  the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  larger-than-expected interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The 50-basis-point cut failed to boost investor confidence \par \par \uc2  and instead backed views in the market that the ECB was behind \par \par \uc2  the curve. The ECB's minimum bid rate now stands at 3.25 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2  The move, however, has raised hopes the combined easing in \par \par \uc2  the U.S. and Europe would help global economy climb out of the \par \par \uc2  severe downturn in coming months. \par \par \uc2  Those hopes and continued equity-related inflows could help \par \par \uc2  Korean won and Taiwan dollar which saw two-month and four-month \par \par \uc2  peaks respectively on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The won's upmove was also supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \par \par \uc2  Korea's views that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was expected to \par \par \uc2  maintain stability on sustained dollar oversupply. \par \par \uc2  Players in the Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso would \par \par \uc2  continue to focus on flows and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to aid the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mired in domestic economic and political woes. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won gapped higher at the open on the lingering cheer \par \par \uc2  from the Bank of Korea's optimistic outlook for the won, \par \par \uc2  breaking the 1,285 level for the first time since September 12. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea kept rates steady on Thursday because of \par \par \uc2  recent hopeful signs for the Korean economy. And despite \par \par \uc2  issuing a warning about future downside risks, it predicted \par \par \uc2  that the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would remain steady \par \par \uc2  thanks to dollar inflows. \par \par \uc2      For several weeks, foreign investors have been on a buying \par \par \uc2  spree of Korean stocks. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar edged higher on hopes of continued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-linked foreign inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net buyers of 2.36 billion Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar worth of local stocks on Thursday, after selling a net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 511 million Taiwan dollars on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched a four-month high on Thursday before\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pulled it down to the well-worn range around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said as the Taiwan dollar was seen as a barometer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of investor confidence on the economy, the approaching\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elections could mean authorities would look for a measured\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given the weak external and domestic conditions such an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation was unlikely to help the economy, an analyst at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. bank in Singapore warned, saying players should be looking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at buying dollars at dips.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar edged slightly lower, hovering just above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8200 in early thin trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was pressured partly by rumoured\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purchases of the euro and the baht by local investors, possibly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to invest in assets there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Local names and U.S. names were also heard buying the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar from 1.8165. However, dealers said the U.S. dollar was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely to sail through 1.8200 without difficulty given\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential profit taking around that level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht found a toehold around 44.45 after a stop-loss was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered at 44.60 in the previous session, but charts show the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar should be well-supported at 44.40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said offshore buying of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. dollar and the Sing dollar might be linked to foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors' plans to buy shares of state-owned Petroleum\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Authority of Thailand (PTT) later this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PTT is expected to raise up to 32 billion baht (US$719\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million) from its IPO by offering up to 920 million shares to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the public at 31-35 each during November 15-21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said apart from technical factors, the dollar/baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par should also be supported by the fact that baht funding costs in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the offshore market has eased.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The one-month forward rate fell to 6/10 satang per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from around 10/15 earlier this week. The 12-month rate remained\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par firm at 125/150 satang.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah steadied itself right above the 10,500 level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after days of suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News that international donors granted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  $3.73\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in aid on Thursday gave the rupiah only a slight boost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because it was long expected. Though donors aired their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par complaints about Jakarta's haphazard approach to reform, there\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was little doubt the aid money would be granted given the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par precarious state of Indonesia' stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moreover, Indonesia is also the world's most populous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nation, adding to its geopolitical importance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, sentiment towards the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had yet to turn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around because of the challenges that the government has to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tackle. On top of that, dealers in Jakarta said Bank Indonesia\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has been the only supplier of the dollar in recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said local corporates may look to pick up dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around these levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was expected to edge higher on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seasonal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows from overseas workers and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lack of dollar demand from local corporates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said most interbank players were trimming\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their long dollar positions amid fears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seek some strengthening of the peso encouraged by the overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remittances ahead of Christmas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said re-introduction of a tiering scheme for overnight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par borrowing, abolished last August to stem speculation against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso, may result in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  becoming more active\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which slashed its key rates by 50 basis\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par points on Thursday said it expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stay stable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the next two months.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0132 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.13       120.74         +0.51\par  Sing dlr      1.8193       1.8166         -0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       34.510         +0.15\par  Korean won   1275.00      1287.40         +0.97\par  Baht           44.46        44.47         +0.02\par  Peso           51.70        51.73         +0.06\par  Rupiah      10450.00     10445.00         -0.05\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.13       114.45         -4.73\par  Sing dlr      1.8193       1.7365         -4.55\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       32.900         -4.53\par  Korean won   1275.00      1277.00         +0.16\par  Baht           44.46        43.70         -1.71\par  Peso           51.70        50.75         -1.84\par  Rupiah      10450.00      9470.00         -9.38\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011109dxb9003uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
