\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Higher As Donors Support '02 Budget \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2001\par 10:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed higher against the dollar Thursday after international donors pledged $3.14 billion to help finance the 2002 budget deficit, traders said. \par \par \uc2  After touching an intraday high of 10,600 rupiah, the dollar closed at IDR10,485 compared with IDR10,638 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  News that Indonesia will receive the funds from international donors for next year's budget lifted sentiment toward the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Jemal-ud-din Kassum, the World Bank's East Asia and Pacific vice president, said the funds reflect the commitment of the lenders toward Indonesia, under the Consultative Group On Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  However, he said they had also urged the Indonesian government to work quickly on reforms to help spur an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "It's very good news for \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to bring the dollar back below IDR10,500. \par \par \uc2  They said further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep the pair in a IDR10,400 to IDR10,500 range Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Leigh Murray, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; leigh.murray@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011108dxb8000l7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
