\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Rangebound, focus on central banks,. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2001\par 03:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were confined \par \par \uc2  to a tight range in early trade on Thursday with many players \par \par \uc2  sidelined ahead of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate-setting meetings \par \par \uc2  in Europe, South Korea and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2      Most dealers were expecting the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) \par \par \uc2  to cut interest rates by 25 basis points on the view that it is \par \par \uc2  behind the curve on monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      In Korea, a Reuters poll showed nine out of 10 economists \par \par \uc2  forecast the Bank of Korea's monetary policy committee would \par \par \uc2  leave its key overnight call rate unchanged at 4.0 percent. \par \par \uc2      They said a recent fresh batch of healthy data is likely to \par \par \uc2  take pressure off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower borrowing costs for \par \par \uc2  this month. \par \par \uc2      But dealers reckoned the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut \par \par \uc2  its key overnight borrowing and lending rates after the Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve's reduction on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      The two-day meeting between the Indonesian government and \par \par \uc2  donors, which come under the umbrella of Consultative Group of \par \par \uc2  Indonesia, ends on Thursday. Jakarta is seeking $3-4 billion in \par \par \uc2  fresh aid from its donors. \par \par \uc2      The government's failure so far to sell its assets and \par \par \uc2  privatise state firms to secure much-needed funds to plug its \par \par \uc2  budget deficit has proven to be a contentious issue with donors \par \par \uc2  and lenders who are concerned about the country's fiscal \par \par \uc2  stability. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was holding up rather well, thanks to suspected\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Since Tuesday, when it touched the 11,000 mark for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first time since July 23, the rupiah has strengthened by some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has spent a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relatively huge amount of dollars to defend the rupiah. A\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European bank dealer estimated the bank unloaded over $50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million on Wednesday. Bank Indonesia had $29.46 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par international reserves as of the third week of October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, dealers said local corporates were likely to pick up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars around 10,500, adding the rupiah's outlook was still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poor given that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the only source of dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supply. THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht followed the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a dearth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fresh local leads, with dealers expecting it to be confined\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts show that the dollar/baht would run into some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resistance at 44.68 which represents the 38.2 retracement of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar/baht's July 23-September 12 downmove.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The latest RSI reading indicated the dollar/baht is still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading in neutral territory, but heading toward the oversold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par line of 30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Bangkok said players were likely to pick up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars on its way down below 44.60, given baht funding costs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have eased.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the offshore market, funding costs have eased markedly,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the one-month forward rate at 5/15 satang per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso opened slightly firmer at 51.87 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar compared with Thursday's close of 51.88, capitalising on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remittances from overseas Filipino workers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sentiment was also boosted by the government's optimistic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast for the third quarter growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Socio-Economic Secretary Dante Canlas said on Wednesday he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected annual gross domestic product growth in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par July-September period to exceed the initial forecast of 2.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to pare\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its benchmark rates further by 25 basis points when they meet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar gained a bit more confidence thanks to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the steady yen, with sentiment also cheered by forthcoming bond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par issues by local companies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore Telecommunications said on Wednesday it planned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to raise the equivalent of $1.5 billion in its debut global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bond offering, though the size, structure, timing, and\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were not given.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore Airlines and local rail operator SMRT Corp also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plan to launch bond issues of S$800 million and S$300-S$500\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million, respectively.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said these bond issues would help to support the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local dollar for now, with the market looking to sell the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on rallies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar rose slightly on the back of local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains, mindful that the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was keeping a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close watch over it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Since late October, the Taiwan dollar has been idling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 34.52 after trading in an increasingly narrow range in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore say the market is reluctant to push\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the exchange rate either way given the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's almost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily presence in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts say the bank is eager to maintain a stable rate to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ensure competitiveness and domestic confidence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indeed, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts have been so successful\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that it was able to cut interest rates without moving the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exchange rate much.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The bank eased key interest rates by 25 basis points to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record lows on Wednesday in a move to further boost domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence. Analysts say the bank's easing has primarily helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par avert a liquidity crunch given the number of bad loans in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0138 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.22       121.01         -0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.8137       1.8171         +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.455       34.520         +0.19\par  Korean won   1290.00      1292.30         +0.18\par  Baht           44.60        44.62         +0.04\par  Peso           51.84        51.88         +0.08\par  Rupiah      10540.00     10625.00         +0.81\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.22       114.45         -5.58\par  Sing dlr      1.8137       1.7365         -4.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.455       32.900         -4.51\par  Korean won   1290.00      1277