\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Steady on yen, but rupiah upset. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2001\par 10:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drew \par \par \uc2  some strength from a steadier yen on Monday, but there \par \par \uc2  was no stopping for the Indonesian rupiah, which slid to fresh \par \par \uc2  three-month lows. \par \par \uc2      Despite dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rupiah \par \par \uc2  fumbled as the World Bank expressed disappointment with \par \par \uc2  Jakarta's progress on reforms in a report ahead of a donors' \par \par \uc2  meeting later in the week. \par \par \uc2      Gains in most regionals were also limited as a grim \par \par \uc2  economic outlook for the region attracted dollar bids at dips. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar, after its sharp rebound from almost \par \par \uc2  four-month lows beyond 1.8350, met dollar demand from local \par \par \uc2  companies just below the 1.8100 level. \par \par \uc2      Equity-linked inflows helped the Korean won and Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar hold steady, but both were locked in recent narrow \par \par \uc2  ranges as the market waited for the policy-setting meeting of \par \par \uc2  the Federal Reserve due Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  With the Fed widely expected to slash its 2.50 percent key \par \par \uc2  fund rate by an aggressive 50 basis points, regional players \par \par \uc2  preferred to wait and watch for a response from local \par \par \uc2  authorities. \par \par \uc2  Withering hopes of a rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  this week and a report indicating European governments could be \par \par \uc2  masking the true extent of their budget deficits pulled down \par \par \uc2  the euro to one-week lows against the dollar and the \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar managed to regain some ground against the yen \par \par \uc2  but struggled to make headway as players doubted a rate cut, \par \par \uc2  the tenth this year, would have a near-term impact on the \par \par \uc2  gloomy economic situation. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped slow the \par \par \uc2  losses, but failed to halt the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market \par \par \uc2  to sell U.S. dollars at 10,650 and 10,800. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \par \par \uc2  countered by strong corporate dollar demand, however. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth sharp fluctuations in the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, it said it had no immediate target for the rupiah, \par \par \uc2  which lost almost two percent on Monday, adding its foreign \par \par \uc2  reserves could not be used excessively. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was hit by a slew of negative news ranging from \par \par \uc2  a rating downgrade to concerns over huge debt loads. Standard \par \par \uc2  and Poor's on Friday cut Indonesia's long-term sovereign debt \par \par \uc2  rating to 'CCC' from 'CCC Plus' and also revised down its \par \par \uc2  outlook to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was off its intraday high after players \par \par \uc2  took advantage of the U.S. dollar's pullback and bought the \par \par \uc2  U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on dips. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore \par \par \uc2  (MAS) might have had a hand in propping up the Sing dollar on \par \par \uc2  Friday night to keep it steady amid M&A talk and ahead of \par \par \uc2  elections. \par \par \uc2  "We would buy U.S. dollar/Sing dollar at 1.8129-1.8170, \par \par \uc2  stop out at 1.8070, with a target of 1.8350," the Bank of \par \par \uc2  America said in a daily note. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was now focused on a new cabinet \par \par \uc2  lineup. Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong, whose People's Action \par \par \uc2  Party enjoys a strong mandate, is expected to announce the new \par \par \uc2  cabinet on November 23. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, flush liquidity and deepening economic \par \par \uc2  gloom has kept short-dated SIBORs low. However, since they have \par \par \uc2  adjusted down quite substantially recently, their downside \par \par \uc2  should be limited from here. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was trapped in a narrow range of 44.63 to 44.73, \par \par \uc2  with corporate dollar demand countered by dollar offers from \par \par \uc2  exporters. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was underpinned by high baht funding costs in \par \par \uc2  the offshore market caused by a recent liquidity squeeze. \par \par \uc2      The one-month forward rate was quoted at 12/17 satang per \par \par \uc2  dollar and the 12-month rate at 140/170 satang. \par \par \uc2      Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula reiterated \par \par \uc2  on Monday that current interest rates were at appropriate \par \par \uc2  levels, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not ease policy in \par \par \uc2  case of a further rate reduction by the Fed on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso notched slightly higher in thin trade thanks to a \par \par \uc2  trickle of dollar inflows from local banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually enjoys gains \par \par \uc2  ahead of Christmas because Filipino overseas workers remit \par \par \uc2  their earnings home. \par \par \uc2  "If you want to buy dollars, do it at lower levels because \par \par \uc2  the peso should strengthen ahead of Christmas," said a local \par \par \uc2  bank dealer in Manila. \par \par \uc2      Still, they said the country's poor fundamentals continued \par \par \uc2  to nag the peso, limiting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside. \par \par \uc2      Moreover, the market was keenly watching the Fed's meeting \par \par \uc2  on Tuesday because it feels the Fed's decision may influence \par \par \uc2  whether the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts rates. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier in the day better than \par \par \uc2  expected inflation in October, coupled with a Fed rate cut, may \par \par \uc2  give it room to slash its overnight borrowing and lending \par \par \uc2  rates, which now stand at 8.75 percent and 11.0 percent. \par \par \uc2      It will hold its weekly monetary board meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won slipped slightly in a thin market with most players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sticking to the sidelines ahead of the FOMC.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea was scheduled to have its monthly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary board meeting on Thursday, and analysts were divided\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as to whether it will cut its overnight call rate. While the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government is eager to boost growth, it is also mindful of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation. Still, inflation fell 0.4 percent in October on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month, giving the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  some room to ease.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign equity flows and a stable yen helped the won resist\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further falls.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar remained true to its recent range of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 34.52, with already slow market activity moving at an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par even more sluggish pace.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Interest in the Taiwan dollar has dwindled in recent weeks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par given the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near daily, and formidable, presence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Balancing the need for a competitive exchange rate and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic confidence, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has trained the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar to stick within a very tight range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Even in the offshore non-deliverable forward market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activity was at best subdued, dealers in Singapore said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0843 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.74       121.74         +0.00\par  Sing dlr      1.8186       1.8311         +0.69\par  Taiwan dlr    34.526       34.528        