\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE1-Bank Indonesia says no immediate target for rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2001\par 08:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Nov 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to smooth out sharp fluctuations in the rupiah but said it had no immediate target for the brittle \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Buffeted by a spate of recent poor economic news, the rupiah weakened further on Monday, approaching 11,000 to the dollar, having lost nearly all its gains since the day President Megawati Sukarnoputri took power in late July. \par \par \uc2  Senior deputy bank governor Anwar Nasution said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves could not be used excessively to support the unit. By 0640 GMT it was being quoted at 10,850/10,900 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "(We) will keep doing it (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) but cannot use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves excessively," Nasution told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  When asked if there was any plan to prevent the rupiah from hitting 11,000, Nasution added: "There is no such target. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we do is aimed at preventing drastic fluctuations. That's it." \par \par \uc2  Nasution said any measure to strengthen the rupiah would not just depend on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also needed government action on economic reforms such as privatisation along with asset sales by the bank restructuring agency (IBRA). \par \par \uc2  "(Investors) are worried about whether we are serious in our privatisation programme and in the sale of IBRA assets," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said problems with the government's privatisation and restructuring plans was dampening sentiment. Not a cent has been raised from privatisation this year. \par \par \uc2  In a blow for that programme, West Sumatra province last week unilaterally took over a unit of state-run Semen Gresik to stop its acquisition by Mexican cement giant Cemex. Cemex is trying to buying a majority stake in Gresik. \par \par \uc2  In addition, the World Bank on Monday expressed disappointment with Jakarta's progress on it latest pact of reforms with the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the rupiah's fall on Monday was also partly due to a Standard & Poor's credit rating downgrade. \par \par \uc2  S&P on Friday cut Indonesia's long term sovereign debt rating to 'CCC' from 'CCC Plus' and also revised down the outlook to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011105dxb500dw5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
