\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weak, but soft dollar caps downside. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,159 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2001\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 26 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed \par \par \uc2  in narrow ranges on Friday though not far from recent lows, \par \par \uc2  aided by a retreating dollar and squaring of long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2      That pushed the Singapore dollar off its three-month low \par \par \uc2  and kept the Thai baht off 10-week lows hit on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won and the Taiwan dollar continued to benefit \par \par \uc2  from equity-related inflows and dollar sales by exporters for \par \par \uc2  month-end requirements of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But none of that kept the Indonesian rupiah and the \par \par \uc2  Philippine peso from probing weaker levels. Only the fear of, \par \par \uc2  or actual \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , capped their downsides. \par \par \uc2      Data from the region showed further economic deterioration. \par \par \uc2  Singapore reported September manufacturing data, Thailand had \par \par \uc2  its trade numbers upto last month and a poll in Korea showed \par \par \uc2  economists expect industrial output to fall. \par \par \uc2  The dollar struggled in early European trade at its lowest \par \par \uc2  for the day against both the yen and the euro amid a \par \par \uc2  lack of fresh impetus to extend recent gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had set 2-= month highs against the yen on \par \par \uc2  Thursday and near seven-week highs versus the euro earlier this \par \par \uc2  week, cheered by growing resilience in the U.S. stock markets \par \par \uc2  to a seemingly-unending flow of bad news. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar failed to hold onto its overnight \par \par \uc2  gains, slipping close to levels of around 1.8275 seen late on \par \par \uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  After enjoying a brief respite overnight in New York trade, \par \par \uc2  the Sing dollar found itself once again assailed by U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  bids at the start of Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment towards the Sing dollar was still negative, \par \par \uc2  dealers said, given the city-state's bleak economic \par \par \uc2  fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Some in the market were convinced there was still further \par \par \uc2  downside for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \par \par \uc2  Singapore's decision to widen its neutral policy band on the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's economy is open, so the government uses the \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted exchange rate as its main policy tool, and its \par \par \uc2  current neutral stance means it seeks zero appreciation of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, spurred by the struggling economy, the MAS \par \par \uc2  recently decided to widen its trading band, which the market \par \par \uc2  understood as tacit acceptance of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      On the macro front, Singapore reported that manufacturing \par \par \uc2  output fell by 22.3 percent in September on the year. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso touched a new 11-week low amid a lack of dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supply and worries over deteriorating economic fundamentals\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with fresh lending data reflecting a drop in borrowing by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said most players were reluctant to take\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressive positions on fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par That reluctance was reflected in a sharp drop of trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par volume, down to only $38 million, versus $100 million on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  statement showed commercial bank lending had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shrunk 0.3 percent in August from a year ago due to a slowdown\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in business activity, particularly in manufacturing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht loitered in a tight range just shy of lows around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44.90 hit on Thursday supported by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and month-end sale of dollars from exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra reinforced those fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par saying the government would aim to boost exports but would also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seek to keep the baht stable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He, however, added that the recent weakness of the baht was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in line with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The commerce ministry said exports declined 9.95 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September on the year while imports slipped 6.19 percent. For\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the years first nine months, exports were down 3.97 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while imports rose 4.31 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah found itself in trouble again, falling to 10,300\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par before the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rescued it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protect the rupiah after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  succumbed to mounting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar bids.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers were divided whether the bank was in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, with some saying they spotted the bank selling dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 10,270/80, and others saying the bank was not in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been on a steady downtrend since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mid-August, depressed by the troubled economy and the lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows. Dealers in Jakarta said the market was distressed over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news the Indonesian government had missed a deadline in selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a majority stake of state-run cement firm Semen Gresik to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico's Cemex.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won squeezed out more gains, helped in large part by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-linked dollar inflows from foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the past few weeks, the won has been caught between the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downward force of a weaker yen and upward pressure from foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors' net buying of local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investment has overridden a weaker yen for now but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts say the won could fall further if the yen continues to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par flag against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JP Morgan Chase said in a recent note the cross rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between the yen and won has fallen, which could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cause the concern of the Korean authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government is believed to be keen on maintaining a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitive exchange rate given the huge downturn in export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand. Japan and Korea do compete on a number of key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par electronics exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar edged higher backed by continued equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and exporter-linked inflows with more help from a steadier yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It hit a session peak of 34.522 but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted again capping the gains to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors were net buyers of 1.87 billion Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar worth of local shares on Friday, taking up the total to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 15.63 billion over the past six sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Exporters continued to sell their dollars to meet their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month-end requirement for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     While equity inflows into Taiwan's stock market has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exerting upwards pressure on the exchange rate, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had put a lid on its rise to defend export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0822 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.61       122.94         +0.27\par  Sing dlr      1.8269       1.8275         +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.539       34.545         +0.02\par  Korean won   1296.30      1297.00         +0.05\par  Baht           44.80        44.75         -0.11\par  Peso           52.04        51.80         -0.46\par  Rupiah      10250.00     10220.00         -0.29\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.61       114.45         -6.66\par  Sing dlr      1.8269       1.7365         -4.95\par  Taiwan dlr    34.539       32.900         -4.75\par  Korean won   1296.30      1277.00         -1.49\par  Baht           44.80        43.70         -2.46\par  Peso           52.04        50.75         -2.48\par  Rupiah      10250.00      9470.00         -7.61\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.8000         +0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011026dxaq00iiq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
