\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 's c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to help rupiah. \b0\par\par\uc2 128 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2001\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, Oct 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help prop up the sagging rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which earlier tested 10,300 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  By 0638 GMT the rupiah was quoted at 10,250/10,270 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  When asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Governor Sjahril Sabirin said: "Yes, we keep doing it." \par \par \uc2  He did not say when the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  or how much was spent. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah has been hit by anti-American sentiment in the world's largest Muslim country following U.S.-led strikes on Afghanistan earlier this month, but strong local corporate dollar demand is also keeping it under pressure. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011026dxaq00cde\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
