\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Up On Alleged Ctrl Bk Dollar Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2001\par 11:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah recovered its early losses to end slightly up in thin trade Wednesday, due to alleged dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward the session's close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 9,980 rupiah, down from Tuesday's close of IDR10,010. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the day's high of IDR10,088 in early trading. State-owned oil and gas company Pertamina was said to have been buying dollars to finance fuel imports. \par \par \uc2  But Bank Indonesia, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , later stepped in to sell the U.S. unit to push it below the psychologically important level of IDR10,000, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials couldn't be reached to confirm the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed very serious in its efforts to drive the dollar below IDR10,000," said a dealer with a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added that the players were also less jittery about the ongoing anti-U.S. protests in Indonesia as they have been largely kept under control. \par \par \uc2  Police Wednesday fired tear gas to stop Muslim student protesters from entering the parliament complex in Jakarta. They were demanding the government to cut ties with the U.S. following its airstrikes on Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2  Small-scale protests also took place in some Indonesian cities Wednesday, but they were peaceful. \par \par \uc2  Defense Minister Matori Abdul Djalil was quoted by the official Antara news agency as saying that the security forces won't hesitate to take stern action against any violent anti-U.S. protests. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to fall to IDR9,900 Thursday with its upside potential capped at IDR10,100. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011010dxaa000ln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
