\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Fin Min: \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Rate Hike Won't Help IDR \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 06:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Indonesian Finance Minister Boediono said Monday that raising interest rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market won't help the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  He said such moves would have little effect in the current circumstances. "The best thing we can do is maintain the domestic situation so it remains cool and calm," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It's something that we have to face as a reality, that raising interest rates or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be effective to help the rupiah," Boediono told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to an intraday high of IDR10,500 Monday from its close Friday at IDR9,825 on concerns the U.S. military strikes on Afghanistan will spark further anti-U.S. protests in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Boediono's comments come after Bank Indonesia's Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom earlier Monday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to sell dollars cautiously to help the local unit. \par \par \uc2  While raising interest rates is unlikely to help ease the local currrency's slide, rates may still rise as a result of the rupiah's renewed weakness. \par \par \uc2  The weighted average interest rate on one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes rose slightly at last week's auction to 17.59% from 17.57% a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia had been expected to lower the SBI rate if the dollar didn't rise above IDR10,000. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't afford to keep interest rates high because higher rates will jack up the costs of recapitalizing local banks. \par \par \uc2  -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; farida.husna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011008dxa80007m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
