\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rocked by attacks, c.banks lend a hand. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were cowering \par \par \uc2  late Monday following the U.S.-led strikes in Afghanistan, the \par \par \uc2  first step of what may be a lengthy military response to the \par \par \uc2  September 11 attacks on the World Trade Center and the \par \par \uc2  Pentagon. \par \par \uc2      Among the big losers, the Indonesian rupiah hit 10-week \par \par \uc2  lows while the Singapore dollar was only just behind at a \par \par \uc2  nine-week trough. \par \par \uc2   A few of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  avoided steep losses as the threat of \par \par \uc2  official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hung over the markets and many players \par \par \uc2  opted for the sidelines until it became clearer how long the \par \par \uc2  conflict will last. \par \par \uc2      The news on that front left little hope for a quick \par \par \uc2  resolution, with U.S. Defence Secretary Donald Rumsfeld warning \par \par \uc2  there was no magic bullet in the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , called 'Enduring \par \par \uc2  Freedom' and the U.S. government's arch-enemy, Osama bin Laden, \par \par \uc2  vowing no peace for America. \par \par \uc2      Among the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indonesian rupiah \par \par \uc2  suffered the most as local banks and corporates rushed to buy \par \par \uc2  dollars amid growing fears that Muslim extremists would act on \par \par \uc2  their threats to expel foreigners in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah's troubles also dogged the Singapore dollar as \par \par \uc2  the city-state is viewed as being vulnerable to unrest in \par \par \uc2  Indonesia given its physical proximity. The Sing dollar also \par \par \uc2  has the misfortune of being a proxy for other Southeast Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as its market is the most liquid in the region. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah shed over a 1,000 rupiah to the dollar at one\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stage to lows around 10,550 as local players rushed to buy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars amid growing fears that Muslim radicals will carry out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their threat to drive out foreigners.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Since the September 11 attacks, a small but strident\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par minority of Muslim extremists have threatened to kick out\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners if the U.S. struck Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With the U.S.-led military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now underway, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market was skittish that these fringe groups may act, providing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par another excuse for foreign investors to avoid Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said the scramble for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steamrolled over Bank Indonesia's attempts to break the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah's fall. The bank was spotted selling $2-3 million around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10,300/350. Later, the rupiah was pulled off its lows thanks to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit-taking on the dollar, which had risen by as much as six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent during the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vowed to protect the rupiah, saying it would\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. But the bank's governor added it did\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not have immediate plans to hike interest rates, which are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par already at two-year highs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country's Finance Minister said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates were unlikely to help, and stressed the need to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par maintain domestic stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar stumbled to a near nine-week low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7965 as the troubles in Indonesia rattled investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The main cause for alarm was fears that any unrest in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia following the U.S. military strikes in Afghanistan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could spill over into Singapore. Dealers said commercial demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for dollars also drove the Sing dollar down, with stop-loss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar buy orders triggered when it skidded past the 1.79 mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Others, however, said the dollar's run against the Sing was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an overreaction as Singapore, a small city-state, is not an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par obvious target even though it is surrounded by predominantly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Muslim countries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "It's really not too clever to buy dollar/Sing right now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because if you step back you would realise how expensive it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is," said a U.S. bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indeed, charts showed the dollar/Sing was in overbought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory, suggesting there was room for the dollar to correct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the next few sessions. By late Monday, it had a 14-day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relative strength index reading of around 85.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht weakened against the dollar as U.S. names and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par other onshore players were heard building long dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the absence of fundamentals that argue for a stronger local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the weaker baht was likely to reduce the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chances of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cutting interest rates. Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on Monday he saw\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par no need for Thailand to cut rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "No need to cut rates because Libor (the one-month London\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank offered rate) is still higher than 2.5 percent. There\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is no point of cutting rates," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Libor is a benchmark rate for the eurodollar and currently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stands at about 2.56 percent. Thailand's benchmark 14-day repo\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate currently stands at 2.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai government has expressed concerns that lower rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could trigger capital outflows and destabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won piggybacked on a firmer yen and rose a notch to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,311.6 from Friday's close of 1,312.2.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was light and orderly, with players showing little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reaction to the U.S.-led military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers also said players were probably on their best\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par behaviour after the government said before the market's open it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it spotted volatility in the exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso trailed lower after the other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept it from falling past 51.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the bank offered around $5-10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped to 51.60 - a level where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most in the market expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . With turnover of only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $48 million, the bank was able to stave off further losses for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was also aided by the fact that corporate dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand was muted, partly because many local corporates had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par already hedged their dollar needs. Dealers added the U.S.-led\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strike was long expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sentiment towards the peso, however, continued to sag given\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's dismal economic outlook and expectations of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. recession.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar closed at 34.557, little moved from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's close of 34.559 as players barely blinked at events on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the global and domestic fronts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Volumes are pitiful. My feeling is that the market has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par already digested the bad news from home, and are just happy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sitting on their dollar longs," said a European bank forwards\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the island's exports fell by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par massive 42.5 percent in September from the same period a year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ago, against expectations of a 36.8 percent fall. Imports also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suffered, dropping by 40.4 percent year-on-year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ministry added exports were unlikly to post growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par until the third quarter of 2002. Taiwan's economy has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par badly hit by the electronics downturn and a powerful typhoon.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0900 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.80       120.49         +0.58\par  Sing dlr      1.7942       1.7842         -0.56\par  Taiwan dlr    34.557       34.559         +0.01\par  Korean won   1312.20      1311.00         -0.09\par  Baht         