\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets -  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , stocks easier on air strikes. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 11:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks \par \par \uc2  eased on Monday following the overnight air strikes against \par \par \uc2  Afghanistan by the United States and Britain in retaliation for \par \par \uc2  the September 11 attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2      The bombing and missile strikes, which may mark the \par \par \uc2  begining of a long military campaign, were well-anticipated but \par \par \uc2  still raised concerns over economic and political implications \par \par \uc2  and fallout. \par \par \uc2      The markets slipped amid those concerns but as the strikes \par \par \uc2  lacked a shock element and Tokyo was closed for a national \par \par \uc2  holiday, the downside was limited. \par \par \uc2      "The fact that the military response has started was not a \par \par \uc2  major surprise and then Tokyo is out....the markets are much \par \par \uc2  quieter," said David Simmonds, Salmon Smith Barney's regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. \par \par \uc2      The yen traded in a narrow range around the 120 mark as \par \par \uc2  players marked the dollar down, reflecting their reluctance to \par \par \uc2  take positions amid the uncertainty. \par \par \uc2      Major Asian equity markets dipped with Hong Kong's Heng \par \par \uc2  Seng down 2.7 percent by midday, Seoul's KOSPI ending off 1.15 \par \par \uc2  percent and Taiwan's TAIEX down 1.82 percent. \par \par \uc2      AUTHORITIES ON ALERT \par \par \uc2      Even more cautious than the market players were the \par \par \uc2  region's central banks, some of whom announced their intention \par \par \uc2  to step into the market to quell any panic. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Korea was the first to issue a warning it would \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2   market. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's cabinet pledged support to its stock market through \par \par \uc2  its stabilisation funds. \par \par \uc2      But while the North Asian central banks were more concerned \par \par \uc2  about the economic implications, analysts said authorities in \par \par \uc2  Indonesia and the Philippines may be more concerned about the \par \par \uc2  political fall out of the U.S.-led \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  "Enduring \par \par \uc2  Freedom". \par \par \uc2      The Indonesian rupiah fell through the 10,000 mark to a \par \par \uc2  10-week low of 10,550 as radical Islamic groups in Jakarta \par \par \uc2  threatened to hunt foreigners and destroy foreign targets. \par \par \uc2      Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it planned to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but would avoid hiking interest rates to prop \par \par \uc2  up the rupiah. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Jakarta earlier said Bank Indonesia sold around \par \par \uc2  $2-3 million through brokers at the 10,300/10,350 level. \par \par \uc2      VULNERABLE \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2      Analysts said similar worries would dominate trade in the \par \par \uc2  Philippines. The peso fell just shy of the 51.60 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vulnerability for both \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Philippines \par \par \uc2  will make the much-needed lowering of key interest rates \par \par \uc2  difficult. \par \par \uc2      The Philippines had cut its key overnight rate by 25 \par \par \uc2  basis-points only last week hoping for inflationary pressure to \par \par \uc2  ease and the peso to stabilise around 50-51 range by the end of \par \par \uc2  the year. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight borrowing rate now stands at 8.75 percent \par \par \uc2  and lending rate at 11 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. $0837 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.76       120.49         +0.61\par  Sing dlr      1.7936       1.7842         -0.52\par  Taiwan dlr    34.557       34.559         +0.01\par  Korean won   1312.20      1311.00         -0.09\par  Baht           44.78        44.69         -0.20\par  Peso           51.60        51.57         -0.07\par  Rupiah      10050.00      9830.00         -2.19\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.76       114.45         -4.43\par  Sing dlr      1.7936       1.7365         -3.18\par  Taiwan dlr    34.557       32.900         -4.79\par  Korean won   1312.20      1277.00         -2.68\par  Baht           44.78        43.70         -2.41\par  Peso           51.60        50.75         -1.65\par  Rupiah      10050.00      9470.00         -5.77\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0837 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par 