\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Get by with a little help from yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2001\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 4 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood their \par \par \uc2  ground against the dollar late on Thursday, backed up by the \par \par \uc2  steady yen and, in some cases, their central banks. \par \par \uc2      The market, however, was increasingly divided as to whether \par \par \uc2  the regionals were going to suffer another bout of weakness or \par \par \uc2  manage to hold onto their newfound stability. \par \par \uc2      One group notes that risk aversion after the September 11 \par \par \uc2  attacks struck the dollar and boosted the yen, which helped \par \par \uc2  most regionals, and this aversion could easily return depending \par \par \uc2  on how the U.S. chooses to retaliate. \par \par \uc2      They add the region's still healthy current account \par \par \uc2  surpluses should save the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from further falls. \par \par \uc2      Others who argue that the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will head south \par \par \uc2  point towards the region's shaky growth outlook. They say risk \par \par \uc2  aversion, ultimately, would send investors packing out of Asia, \par \par \uc2  which is not good news in a region parched of foreign inflows. \par \par \uc2  "Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  should get some support from their \par \par \uc2  current account surpluses and the relatively stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  Beyond these assumptions, however, we believe risk aversion \par \par \uc2  will have other, even greater negative implications for \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the months ahead," said JP Morgan Chase in a \par \par \uc2  recent report. \par \par \uc2  Whatever the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  scenario, regional central banks are \par \par \uc2  showing a willingness to ease monetary policy to help cushion \par \par \uc2  their economies. The Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined the ranks \par \par \uc2  of Hong Kong and Taiwan on Thursday when it cut rates by a \par \par \uc2  quarter percentage point. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah crawled back to the right side of 9,700 as talk \par \par \uc2  of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked rounds of dollar \par \par \uc2  unwinding from corporates and interbank players. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was heard selling up to $50 million to \par \par \uc2  drag the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from 9,900. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah was also supported by news that Indonesian Bank \par \par \uc2  Restructuring Agency (IBRA) would stick with its plan to sell \par \par \uc2  51 percent of the country's largest retail bank, Bank Central \par \par \uc2  Asia. \par \par \uc2  On the investment front, foreign investment approvals in \par \par \uc2  Indonesia from January to August fell to $5.75 billion from \par \par \uc2  $7.25 billion in the same period last year, according to data \par \par \uc2  from the Investment Coordinating Board. \par \par \uc2  Investors have reduced their Indonesian exposure since the \par \par \uc2  country plunged into political and economic turmoil in the late \par \par \uc2  1990s and have remained wary ever since. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hovered near the day's trough around 1.7790 \par \par \uc2  as the market remained concerned over the country's economic \par \par \uc2  outlook. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expected Singapore's economy \par \par \uc2  to contract 1.7 percent this year compared with 3.6 percent \par \par \uc2  growth they saw in a June survey. \par \par \uc2  The market is focused on preliminary numbers for third \par \par \uc2  quarter GDP expected on October 7. The market widely \par \par \uc2  anticipates an official downward revision of the forecast. \par \par \uc2  Charts show 1.7842 is a tough barrier for the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar/Sing dollar for now as it represents the 50 percent \par \par \uc2  retracement of the July 16-September 17 U.S. dollar downmove. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was down but off early lows of 1,316 rescued by \par \par \uc2  export-related dollar inflows. Gains in local stock market also \par \par \uc2  helped cap the downside. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said offshore players led the dollar \par \par \uc2  buying in both the spot and non-deliverable forward markets \par \par \uc2  after the three-day Chusok holidays. \par \par \uc2  They reported speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if it decided \par \par \uc2  not to follow others in the region by cutting interest rates, \par \par \uc2  may allow a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy board held a meeting \par \par \uc2  early Thursday but a spokesman said any decision on further \par \par \uc2  rate cuts was unlikely until next week. \par \par \uc2  The short-term call rate is now at a record low of 4.00 \par \par \uc2  percent after a 50 basis point cut in September, the fourth cut \par \par \uc2  this year. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was off its session low of 51.61 helped by talk \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in aid of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \par \par \uc2  its monetary board decided to cut key overnight rates by 25 \par \par \uc2  basis points. \par \par \uc2      Effective Friday the overnight borrowing rate would be \par \par \uc2  lowered to 8.75 percent and lending to 11 percent. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila said they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold \par \par \uc2  dollars in both the non-deliverable and spot markets through \par \par \uc2  two foreign banks. \par \par \uc2      Others said subdued volume of $98.70 million suggested the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not behind the move. The total turnover on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday was $95.60 million. \par \par \uc2      Keeping the upside limited was August export data that \par \par \uc2  showed a decline of 25.73 percent from August last year. The \par \par \uc2  decline was the sharpest drop in 21 years. \par \par \uc2      THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2      The baht lingered around 44.60 weighed down by dollar \par \par \uc2  demand from local corporates and oil companies, after dollar \par \par \uc2  sales by Singapore and Hong Kong names helped it off a low of \par \par \uc2  44.67. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said uncertainty over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  interest rate policy was also prompting offshore players to \par \par \uc2  square out of their long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  The government has repeatedly said it would not cut the \par \par \uc2  benchmark 2.5 percent 14-day repo rate but players believe \par \par \uc2  that, with most regional central banks following in the steps \par \par \uc2  of the Fed, the Bank of Thailand may yet succumb to the siren \par \par \uc2  call. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar stayed in its comfort zone just above \par \par \uc2  34.60 despite another rate cut from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, Singapore dealers said trading in the \par \par \uc2  non-deliverable forward market was active, with dollar-buying \par \par \uc2  particularly strong in the one-month tenor. \par \par \uc2  They said the market was betting that the island's powerful \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would soon let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaken, at least \par \par \uc2  towards 35. \par \par \uc2      The one-month forward was quoted at 0.105/.125 in late \par \par \uc2  trade compared to 0.085/0.095 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its key rates by 0.25 percentage \par \par \uc2  point. It also slashed its reserve requirement ratios to five \par \par \uc2  percent from 6.22 percent and its reserve requirement ratio on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to five percent from 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  All the moves were aimed at boosting the local economy, \par \par \uc2  which the government expects to contract by 0.37 percent this \par \par \uc2  year - Taiwan's first ever full-year contraction. \par \par \uc2  "They're basically saying they want banks to hold onto U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollars. So there's really no other direction for the Taiwan \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but down," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0918 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.47       120.80         +0.27\par  Sing dlr      1.7785       1.7780         -0.03\par  Taiwan dlr    34.568       34.569         +0.00\par  Korean won   1312.00      1318.00         +0.46\par  Baht           44.59        44.71         +0.27\par  