\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firm as dollar wilts against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2001\par 04:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took \par \par \uc2  heart early on Thursday as the yen resisted the dollar's \par \par \uc2  advances despite suprisingly upbeat U.S. services data. \par \par \uc2      While the Singapore dollar and Thai baht trotted after the \par \par \uc2  yen, vigilant central banks in Indonesian and the Philippines \par \par \uc2  were also keeping dollar bulls at bay. \par \par \uc2      Still, dealers said little has changed in sentiment towards \par \par \uc2  the rupiah and peso, which are expected to slowly sink under \par \par \uc2  the weight of sober economic outlooks for those countries. \par \par \uc2      Curiously, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually closely tied to the yen \par \par \uc2  -- the North Asians -- were coming under attack as players \par \par \uc2  focused on their domestic economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      The National Association of Purchasing Management's index \par \par \uc2  of U.S. non-manufacturing activity rose to 50.2 in September \par \par \uc2  from August's 45.5. Wall Street used that bit of news, hopes \par \par \uc2  for a huge stimulus package and a solid earnings outlook from \par \par \uc2  technology heavyweight Cisco to muster a rally. \par \par \uc2  Still, players in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were less \par \par \uc2  sanguine, with many suspecting the services data may not fully \par \par \uc2  reflect the damage done by the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2      The dollar touched a high of around 121.48 yen in overnight \par \par \uc2  trade, before profit-takers chased it below the 121 level. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said with players continuing to book profits from \par \par \uc2  the dollar's two-week rise, most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should enjoy \par \par \uc2  a temporary respite before the region's shaky fundamentals come \par \par \uc2  into view again. \par \par \uc2  With that in mind, more and more Asian central banks have \par \par \uc2  hopped on the rate-cutting bandwagon, with Taiwan's bank \par \par \uc2  cutting interest rates by a quarter percentage point Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will meet later in the day and says \par \par \uc2  a rate cut is up for discussion. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hovered in a 1.7733-1.7776 range, with a \par \par \uc2  steadier yen providing some support. \par \par \uc2  Charts show 1.7842 is a tough barrier for the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar/Sing dollar for now as it represents the 50 percent \par \par \uc2  retracement of the July 16-September 17 U.S. dollar downmove. \par \par \uc2  The market is focused on preliminary figures for third \par \par \uc2  quarter GDP expected on October 7. The market widely expects an \par \par \uc2  official downward revision of the forecast. \par \par \uc2  Some analyst reckoned this might provide a good opportunity \par \par \uc2  for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shift policy to a loosening bias, so \par \par \uc2  implying a weaker Sing$. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  Dollar profit-taking from both offshore and onshore parties \par \par \uc2  helped lift the baht from its overnight trough of 44.82. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/yen direction remains the key factor. Once the \par \par \uc2  yen rebounded against the dollar, players also pared their long \par \par \uc2  dollar/baht positions," said a dealer in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said 44.82 was still a good support for the \par \par \uc2  baht. Charts show a dollar break above that level will complete \par \par \uc2  a double bottom and could lead the dollar/baht much higher. \par \par \uc2      The tom/next rate was quoted at -0.5/-0.3 satang per dollar \par \par \uc2  offshore and -0.10/-0.04 satang onshore. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah held above 9,900 as those with exceedingly long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions unwound the dollar after rumours that Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The stop was triggered at 9,950 yesterday and players are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wary of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Also, the fact that the market is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still very long of dollars underpins the rupiah," said a dealer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at a European bank in Jakarta.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the upside for the rupiah should be capped by lingering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of escalation in anti-U.S. protests and concerns over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible damage to foreign investor perception of the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par judiciary after the acquittal of Tommy Suharto.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was knocked past Friday's closing level of 1,309.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as markets re-opened in Seoul.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers said dollar buying interest in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward market spilled into the spot market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One-month won NDFs rose to as high as 1,320/22 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par before easing to current levels around 1,316/18.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's losses were capped by early gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the local stock market. The benchmark Korean Composite Stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Price Index was up by over three percent, taking its cue from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Nasdaq's overnight rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of Korea said its monetary policy board would meet\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later in the day, but that a decision on rates would likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par come next week. Many analysts believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower its short term call rate, which now stands at 4.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, following the Federal Reserve's latest easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar slipped in early active trade to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.585 following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to slash rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dealers said the market was abuzz as to whether\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the bank was going to match the latest rate cut with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tolerance for a weaker exchange rate. The Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has been actively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to defend the local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But it has been known to drop its defence in the past to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par help the island maintain its export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar-buying interest was the strongest in the one-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forward, which was quoted at 0.085/0.095.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said offshore players were banking on the local\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hitting 35 to the dollar soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered rates by a quarter percentage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par point on Wednesday, stepping up its easing campaign as Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par braces for an expected full-year contraction for 2001 - its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first ever.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso moved languidly around 51.57 as the market puzzled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's next act.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been actively\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to defend the frail peso, making most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players wary of being caught too long on dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was also paying close attention to the bank's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetary board meeting, scheduled for later in the day. Though\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the bank has kept rates steady for months, many in the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have been wondering if the latest Fed cut may inspire the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to also ease its key overnight rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With one government official predicting a rate cut, the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has remained coy as to which way it might swing at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this week's meeting. The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a rate cut may be up for discussion, but that the board\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has to consider inflation and the exchange rate. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. $0213 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.68       120.80         +0.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7753       1.7780         +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.574       34.569         -0.01\par  Korean won   1312.00      1318.00         +0.46\par  Baht           44.60        44.71         +0.25\par  Peso           51.57        51.58         +0.01\par  Rupiah       9850.00      9900.00         +0.51\par  Ringgit       3.7994       3.7998         +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.68       114.45         -5.16\par  Sing dlr      1.7753       1.7365         -2.19\par  Taiwan dlr    34.574       32.900         -4.84\par  Korean won   1312.00      1277.00         -2.67\par  Baht           44.60        43.70         -2.02\par  Peso           51.57        50.75         -1.59\par  Rupiah       9850.00      9470.00         -3.86\par  Ringgit       3.7994       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011004dxa400464\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
