\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up;Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2001\par 12:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended higher Wednesday on what dealers suspect was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a market that was already long in dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 9,915 rupiah, down from its close Tuesday at IDR10,025. \par \par \uc2  Dealers believe that Bank Indonesia persistently sold the dollar above IDR10,000 to help the local unit, although Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't confirm any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  However, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help the local unit. \par \par \uc2  The market was skeptical about the threat as Bank Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves aren't considered substantial. Its gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves amounted to $28.96 billion as of Sept. 28, down $44.5 million from a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Gultom also said Bank Indonesia has enough \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $30 million Wednesday. Dealers also believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold that amount Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Despite the rupiah's gains, a dealer with a foreign bank said "underlying sentiment is still bullish on the dollar." \par \par \uc2  He said the market is still concerned that there will be anti-U.S. protests in Jakarta if the U.S. attacks targets in Afghanistan to retaliate against the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. State Department has warned U.S. citizens not to travel to Indonesia and has pulled nonessential embassy personnel out of the country. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's recent weakness prompted Bank Indonesia to raise the weighted average rate on its one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes to 17.59% in a weekly auction late Wednesday, from 17.57% last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers, however, said the rate hike won't significantly help sentiment towards the rupiah as the market is preoccupied with the possibility of domestic unrest. \par \par \uc2  They expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,850 and IDR10,050 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (CORRECTED 1146GMT) \par \par \uc2  The market was skeptical about the threat as Bank Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves aren't considered substantial. Its gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves amounted to $28.96 billion as of Sept. 28, down $44.5 million from a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  (In an item that ran at 10:40 GMT the drop in foreign reserves was misstated.) \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011003dxa3000lw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
