\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Says Foreign Reserves Enough To Aid Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2001\par 04:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank Indonesia said Wednesday that it has sufficient foreign reserves to support the rupiah, which sank to three-month lows against the U.S. dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We have enough dollars to sell in order to make the market calm," Bank Indonesia deputy governor Miranda Gultom told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's foreign reserves as of Sept. 28 stood at $28.966 billion, which analysts say will likely be inadequate to defend the rupiah in the longer term given huge foreign debt repayment needs. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor, Sjahril Sabirin, also repeated Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular stance that it is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupiah ended at a three-month low of IDR10,025 per dollar Tuesday as the Supreme Court's decision to acquit Tutomo "Tommy" Mandala Putra, the son of former dictator Suharto, of fraud hurt sentiment. The rupiah was also hammered by rising anti-U.S. protests in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around IDR10,003 early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia sold more than $30 million in the market Tuesday, but this failed to help the rupiah because demand for dollars was too strong, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; farida.husna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011003dxa30003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
