\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen dampens spirits in thin holiday trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2001\par 04:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on the \par \par \uc2  defensive early on Monday as the yen stumbled a bit after the \par \par \uc2  release of a dismal Japanese corporate sentiment survey. \par \par \uc2      Trading in the region was light as markets in Hong Kong, \par \par \uc2  Taipei, and Seoul were closed for public holidays, which may \par \par \uc2  help regionals stand their ground as trading interest was \par \par \uc2  modest. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's (BOJ) 'tankan' quarterly survey for \par \par \uc2  September showed sentiment from large manufacturers soured from \par \par \uc2  June, with the big manufacturers' diffusion index coming in at \par \par \uc2  minus 33 against minus 16 in June. \par \par \uc2  Still, the market did expect the grim news and was paying \par \par \uc2  more attention as to whether the BOJ would stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  now \par \par \uc2  that half-year bookclosing was over in Japan. \par \par \uc2  First impressiones were that it would continue to sell yen \par \par \uc2  when needed with Senior Japanese Finance Minsitry official \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi saying on Monday the ministry would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at appropriate times. \par \par \uc2  With recession looming over the region's biggest trading \par \par \uc2  partner, the United States, and its largest economy, Japan, \par \par \uc2  analysts say Asian countries were bracing for a protracted \par \par \uc2  slowdown, if not worse. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the Federal Reserve's policy-setting \par \par \uc2  committee will meet on Tuesday, and is widely expected to cut \par \par \uc2  rates to help steady badly shaken sentiment. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was dragged lower by the yen and the \par \par \uc2  city-state's own troubled economic outlook to hover aorund \par \par \uc2  1.7660. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players were looking to stack up their long \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar positions as the yen was seen as weakening past 120 \par \par \uc2  again. Even more timid players were seeking to buy U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  on dips. \par \par \uc2  Singapore will issue a revised 2001 gross domestic product \par \par \uc2  forecast on Sunday. The market has been chattering as to \par \par \uc2  whether the government will also shift its monetary policy \par \par \uc2  stance to loose from neutral because the economy, which is \par \par \uc2  already in a recession, is expected to see tougher times. \par \par \uc2      Still, the U.S. dollar could run aground at 1.7700, where \par \par \uc2  profit-taking was expected to emerge. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht hovered near 44.50 in sympathy with a weaker yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with activity subdued ahead of the Fed meeting on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts say it is unlikely the Bank of Thailand will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cut its already very low benchmark rate in the near-term even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if the Fed cuts as expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market shrugged aside better than expected trade data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par released on Friday as it is more focused on the ramifications\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the September 11 attacks on the Thai economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Commerce Ministry is expected to release September\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consumer prices later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was weighed by corporate dollar demand and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concerns over potential violence caused by anti-U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protesters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hardline groups in Indonesia have warned of a jihad, or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holy war, if Afghanistan is hit while some have signed up to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fight for Afghanistan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Although the size of the anti-U.S. rallies have been pretty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par small, some investors have taken such developments seriously,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers in Jakarta said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rumoured to have been in the market on Friday, should help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limit losses, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Charts show the dollar/rupiah is still trapped in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par uptrend channel dating back to August 14, indicating further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains are likely for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar barely moved in offshore trade as Taipei\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets were closed for the Mid Autumn Festival. They will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par re-open on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore dealers said there was little trading interest in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the non-deliverable forward market. But they added the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was likely to be hurt by the yen's losses and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par island's economic malaise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was barely traded in the offshore non-deliverable\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forward market due to a long holiday onshore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Korea's financial markets are closed October 1-3 for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chusok or thanksgiving holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They will resume trading on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso is expected to be kept in its recent range, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.40 seen as a good support. It opened at 51.35 compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.32 at the close on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Sunday it expected dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remittances from overseas workers to reach $5.5 to 6 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year, around the same level as a year ago.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Remittances from an estimated seven million Filipinos\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par living or working aboard contribute a vital chunk of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's gross national product.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Meanwhile, the country's external debt rose to $50.89\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion at the end of June, up 1.9 percent from $49.94 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the end of the first quarter. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0155 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.80       119.27         -0.44\par  Sing dlr      1.7662       1.7663         +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       34.548         -0.00\par  Korean won   1299.00      1308.50         +0.73\par  Baht           44.47        44.43         -0.09\par  Peso           51.33        51.32         -0.02\par  Rupiah       9670.00      9700.00         +0.31\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.80       114.45         -4.47\par  Sing dlr      1.7662       1.7365         -1.68\par  Taiwan dlr    34.549       32.900         -4.77\par  Korean won   1299.00      1277.00         -1.69\par  Baht           44.47        43.70         -1.73\par  Peso           51.33        50.75         -1.13\par  Rupiah       9670.00      9470.00         -2.07\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dxa1003e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
