\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ride yen's coat tails, retaliation feared. \b0\par\par\uc2 858 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were choppy \par \par \uc2  on Friday with trade dominated by action in the yen \par \par \uc2  where the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to sell the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Japan had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the third day this week the bank has \par \par \uc2  acted to curb the yen's appreciation. \par \par \uc2      The yen had hit 7-month highs on the dollar around 115.85 \par \par \uc2  late Thursday following steep losses on Wall Street and \par \par \uc2  mounting concerns that last week's assault on the U.S. would \par \par \uc2  push the global economy into recession. \par \par \uc2      President George W. Bush's defiant speech to Congress on \par \par \uc2  Friday also fanned fears that the war against terrorism could \par \par \uc2  be a lengthy one, deepening uncertainties over global markets. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the stronger yen and current account \par \par \uc2  surpluses in Asia should continue to support regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short run, although rising risk aversion \par \par \uc2  would eventually have negative implications for offshore \par \par \uc2  investment in the region. \par \par \uc2      Trading was subdued as investors were reluctant to take new \par \par \uc2  positions aggressively ahead of a fresh batch of data to be \par \par \uc2  released by the U.S. and the region next week. \par \par \uc2      U.S. consumer confidence data, a key leading indicator of \par \par \uc2  economic growth, are out on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar was lower at 1.7420 as gains from U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by a large U.S. name was erased by U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying from a few local banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unlikely to be behind the dollar purchases as the Sing dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the current level was not out of sync with other regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent gains, JP Morgan Chase\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued to suggest that clients short the Sing dollar in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-month forwards against the basket or the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It said the Sing dollar had scope to drop to 1.7800 by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end of October as Singapore's rapidly slowing economy could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prompt the MAS to guide it lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht drifted in a tight range of 44.14-44.25 as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market lacked the resolve to push it out of this band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is rangebound. Players looked to buy the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on dips toward 44.10, but a drop below 44.25 was met promptly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by profit-taking," said a Bangkok dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the domestic front, there was no shortage of bad news.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said on Friday the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government would announce a revised 2002 gross domestic product\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast early next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bangkok Post newspaper quoted Somkid as saying GDP in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2002 might be cut by one or two percentage points from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current target of four to six percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah tracked the regionals higher as those who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overbought the U.S. dollar squared positions ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par actively in the market lately, also gave the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some support, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the money market, Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates unchanged at 15.125 percent for the overnight rate and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 15.875 percent for the 7-day rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates are among the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tools\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to affect liquidity in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Peso trading in the onshore market was close to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par standstill, with a mere $19.50 million transacted compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average normal daily turnover of $80-100 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trapped in a narrow 51.29-51.40 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the market was pretty squarish and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players were reluctant to take fresh positions amid fears the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. might strike back as early as this weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won ended weaker against the dollar on Friday on steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar purchases from importers and local stock sales by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign equity investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors sold a net of 50.3 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local shares on Friday, extending their net selling to five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the won's downside in the near-term is likely to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited by seasonal dollar sales by exporters toward the end of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the month, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0925 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.28       117.34         +0.91\par  Sing dlr      1.7430       1.7419         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.573       34.575         +0.01\par  Korean won   1295.00      1298.50         +0.27\par  Baht           44.15        44.20         +0.11\par  Peso           51.19        51.29         +0.20\par  Rupiah       9410.00      9450.00         +0.43\par  Ringgit       3.7995     