\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Down As Debt Problems Weigh \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 11:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended down Wednesday on corporate demand for dollars, but off its day lows as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently sold dollars to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted between 9,590 rupiah and IDR9,640 late Wednesday, much higher than IDR9,520 to IDR9,560 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched an intraday high of IDR9,760 as local companies bought dollars to repay debt or fund imports. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia stepped in during thin afternoon trading to sell about $20 million through brokers, Jakarta-based bankers said. \par \par \uc2  "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if necessary," Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin told reporters Wednesday. The bank's policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but not to comment on any particular action. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to help in the long term, with the rupiah remaining under pressure from debt repayment, traders said. Public debt alone is equal to a year's gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah is also facing pressure from fears any retaliation by the U.S. for last week's terrorist attacks could incite further unrest in Indonesia, the world's most populous Muslim nation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia, or SBI, note yielded 17.66% at Wednesday's auction, unchanged from a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Governor Sjahril said Wednesday the bank won't raise rates further, but at the same time added that Indonesia was unlikely to follow the U.S. Federal Reserve's 50-basis-point rate cut to 3% earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia is trying to cut rates to help ease the pressure of funding its budget deficit from domestic bonds. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want to see the rate go too low as inflationary pressures remain in the economy. The rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still relatively weak against the dollar, which makes imported goods more expensive. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is likely to trade in a range between IDR9,575 and IDR9,750 Thursday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010919dx9j000li\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
