\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Softer, eye Japan moves to curb yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 18 (Reuters) - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  softened early on Tuesday after the dollar held up despite \par \par \uc2  sharp falls on Wall Street, thanks in part to Japanese efforts \par \par \uc2  to rein in the yen . \par \par \uc2   The Bank of Japan (BOJ) flexed its muscles on Monday, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in nearly a year to try and halt \par \par \uc2  a damaging rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also won the \par \par \uc2  tacit approval of U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill who said \par \par \uc2  it was appropriate for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2      The focus now is the BOJ's monetary policy meeting, which \par \par \uc2  runs from today to Wednesday, with expectations high it will \par \par \uc2  follow the lead of the Federal Reserve and ease further. \par \par \uc2      "I think the BOJ will be serious about taking more action \par \par \uc2  on the yen as, though the U.S. is suffering, Japan's economy is \par \par \uc2  suffering more," said a senior analyst from a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2      "But it is difficult to tell how successful it (BOJ) will \par \par \uc2  be and what the exact effect would be on the regionals," he \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      Efforts to curb the yen coupled with aversion to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar given economic conditions and last week's recent terror \par \par \uc2  attacks could still benefit the euro -- an important component \par \par \uc2  for the Singapore dollar's trade weighted basket, he said. \par \par \uc2      Rate cuts by central banks in the United States, Europe and \par \par \uc2  Canada overnight suggested similar moves by certain countries \par \par \uc2  in the region sometime soon. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong had already eased by 50 basis points and \par \par \uc2  economists said the Philippines was likely to move soon, \par \par \uc2  possibly followed by South Korea. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan's financial markets are closed for a second day as \par \par \uc2  the island begins a massive clean-up in the wake of Typhoon \par \par \uc2  Nari which flooded the capital and killed at least 30 people. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar headed south to 1.7365 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following the concerted rate cuts abroad, with market talk\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par centred on rumours the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS) had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the local unit continued to trade at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong end of the MAS' assumed trading range and that the bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was likely to lead the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower following rate cuts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par abroad.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There is talk of official buying of dollars as the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looks as though it has a lot more room to depreciate," said a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer from a European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "With all the central banks cutting rates, the MAS is bound\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to weaken the Sing. We're looking for 1.7420 today," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to trade between 1.7350 and 1.7450\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the coming days if the G3 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to hover\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around current levels, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won opened barely changed at 1,298.5 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the Monday's close of 1,298.7 as players took a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wait-and-see stance ahead of the BOJ meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to move in a narrow range, caught\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between hopes of capital inflows and importer hedging activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after it touched an intraday low of 1,300 the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     There were unconfirmed rumours that General Motors (GM.N)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would be signing a memorandum of understanding for its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prospective purchase of Daewoo Motors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Korea vice governor Park Chul said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had no plans to convene a monetary policy board meeting ahead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of its next scheduled meeting on October 11.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But analysts said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policymakers could still opt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for an early rate cut as last week's terror attacks on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par United States, a main destination for Korea exports, were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poised to tip Korea's feeble economy into a downward spiral.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah dipped to a five-week low around 9,400,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triggered by dollar buying from foreign banks and corporates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading conditions remained thin, with deals largely driven\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by commercial needs, exaggerating volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they expected more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Bank\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after it appeared to enter the market at the 9,260\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level on Monday. As a result, the rupiah was unlikely to fall\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par much below 9,400 in the near-term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's bank restructuring agency said on Monday that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it plans to sell assets worth $1.04 billion through open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par auction before the end of the year to help plug the state's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gaping budget deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht pulled back to 44.10 per dollar so surrendering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most of MOnday's gains, as the market paused for fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par directions after the Fed's aggressive rate cut and ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOJ's policy meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was also talk the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday to buy the dollar below 44.00 after one Japanese bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which normally deals on behalf of the Bank of Thailand was seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A strong baht could hurt the country's exports which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par account for almost 60 percent of its gross domestic product.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The one-month forward rate rose to 8/13 satang for dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore and 1.25/1.75 satang onshore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso tracked the regionals lower to opened at 51.35 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par light trading compared with the Monday's close of 51.26.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Players were cautious ahead of a special Monetary Board\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting later in the day. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Buenaventura said the bank would convene the meeting to discuss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par what policy move to take following the Fed's cut, with much\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speculation they will deliver an easing of their own.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's overnight borrowing rate is currently at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9.0 percent and the lending rate is at 11.25 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.78       118.96         +1.00\par  Sing dlr      1.7360       1.7370         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.575       34.579         +0.01\par  Korean won   1298.00      1290.00         -0.62\par  Baht           44.10        44.29         +0.43\par  Peso           51.33        51.27         -0.12\par  Rupiah       9310.00      9098.00         -2.28\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change