\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Pare early gains after Japan buys dlrs. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,078 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2001\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  gave up earlier gains fuelled by dollar bears on Monday after \par \par \uc2  Japan's monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in \par \par \uc2  nearly a year to try and halt a damaging rise in the yen \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2      The regionals had been p(ushing higher as the dollar \par \par \uc2  suffered across the board but a fall to seven-month lows under \par \par \uc2  117.00 yen sparkled the Japanese into selling yen for \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Japan was believed to have bought up to at \par \par \uc2  least $1.0 billion to curb the yen's strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But with only limited success since in late trade the dollar \par \par \uc2  had faded back to 117.15 yen from highs around 118. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not come as a surprise given that \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials had expressed a desire to see a weaker yen \par \par \uc2  to help Japan's economy avoid recession. \par \par \uc2      Falling Asian stock markets ahead of a resumption of trade \par \par \uc2  in U.S. equities later on Monday also weighed on the regionals, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      "Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have given back most of their recent \par \par \uc2  gains, underscoring the fact that they probably should weaken \par \par \uc2  from here," said an economist from a European bank. \par \par \uc2      "As soon as we see some stability in the United States, the \par \par \uc2  focus will be back on fundamentals in Asia which will remain \par \par \uc2  weak for some time to come," he said. \par \par \uc2      The market is waiting anxiously to see if the Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve cut rates to boost sentiment, with an imminent easing \par \par \uc2  of at least 25 basis point already factored in, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan's financial markets remained shut on Monday as \par \par \uc2  Typhoon Nari pounded the island, killing at least 21 people and \par \par \uc2  bringing floods to the capital Taipei. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht was a shade firmer against the dollar at 43.98,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but was still struggling to break convincingly above the key 44\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Investors were selling the dollar against regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the yen showed its resilience despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also supported by second quarter domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic data which fared better than expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country's gross domestic product (GDP) grew 0.9 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter-on-quarter during April-June after a revised and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seasonally adjusted 0.1 percent quarterly decline in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previous quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Sing dollar retained its firm tone at 1.7315 despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bearish export data, but was trading below its intraday high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1.7300.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was underpinned by its safe haven\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par status within the region and the view that local companies have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par become more risk averse and scaled back on their plans to buy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore's non-oil domestic exports in August took another\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beating, contracting 29.9 percent on the year in norminal terms\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 27.2 percent in real terms, within broad market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But we are afraid that the worst may not yet be over.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Obviously, demand from the U.S. will be affected by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par incidents on September 11. The future of world trade is likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to suffer should the conflict widen and prolong," said Syetarn\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hansakul, economist at WestLB.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won softened after the Bank of Japan's dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  capped the yen's rapid appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended at 1,298.7 per dollar in thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade compared with 1,290.0 at the start and 1,296.3 at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said apart from the yen's strength, there was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par little reason to justify further gains in the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The prospect of a combination of much slower growth and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher oil prices, in the case of sustained U.S. military\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par action against terrorism, should weigh on Asian economies,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par including oil-dependent Korea, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIA RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah hurtled through the 9,300 level for the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par time since early August as foreign banks and corporates soaked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par up dollars partly for genuine commercial needs, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One dealer said that foreign banks had bid for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par throughout the day despite expectations that Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up the rupiah at around 9,200 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "BI did appear to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 9,260 today but it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had no impact," said the dealer from a different European bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "People just thought it was a good bet to but dollar/rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though there is no specific news," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Like stock markets elsewhere, Jakarta sank more than four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent amid fears that U.S. markets might fall sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they expected the rupiah's downside to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited to around 9,400 in the near-term given BI's intent to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso slipped to 51.25 per dollar after a drop in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic stocks to a fresh 35-month low combined painfully with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Despite the sour tone, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained within the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confines of its recent range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economists said all eyes were on whether the Fed would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announce a further cut in rates ahead of its October 2 policy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting, given that the Philippines was likely to be the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian country to follow with a rate cut.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippines has already hinted that there may be a need\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to lower rates, with its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying it would like to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par carefully assess "imminent inflation threats that could arise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from, among other things, a sustained increase in world oil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices."\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0859 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.33       118.91         +1.35\par  Sing dlr      1.7313       1.7371         +0.34\par  Taiwan dlr    34.575       34.579         +0.01\par  Korean won   1298.50      1295.00         -0.27\par  Baht           43.98        44.22         +0.55\par  Peso     