\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian Rupiah Ends Higher On Central Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 11:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed higher against the dollar Friday due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 8,860 rupiah, down from IDR8,920 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Shortly after trading began, local companies bought dollars to repay maturing offshore debts, pushing the unit to its intraday high of IDR9,025. \par \par \uc2  But Bank Indonesia stepped in to sell dollars, dealers said. They predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $20 million Friday. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Sjahril Sabirin admitted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah earlier this week but he didn't comment on Friday's move. Its dollar purchases were, howevever, confirmed by commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked dollar selling by banks, but there was plenty of dollar demand near IDR8,825," said a dealer with a foreign bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market shrugged off a 0.21% on-month deflation in August, choosing to focus on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR8,800 and IDR8,900 Monday, with Bank Indonesia supporting the rupiah near the IDR9,000 to a dollar level. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-