\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Stick to safe ranges. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,056 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2001\par 10:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 30 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved a little to the right and a little to the left, only to end up stuck in their recent ranges late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts blamed their indecisive movements on persistently wobbly sentiment towards the dollar, and the yen's failure to take advantage of that sentiment. Those conflicting factors have sent players to the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  While the Singapore dollar tagged after the yen, other usually yen-sensitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Korean won and Taiwan dollar were cowed by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Both the Korean and Taiwan central banks are believed to be keen on maintaining export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The market was waiting for the day's major event - the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting, which was expected to produce a 25 basis-point cut. A decision is expected at 1145 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A cut aimed at boosting growth in the euro-zone could help the euro rise. That in turn could help the Singapore dollar as the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to be a significant component in its trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso failed to react to better than expected second quarter gross domestic product data. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, Hong Kong will issue its second-quarter numbers and Korea will release July industrial output as well as Auguust consumer price data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht extended early losses to trade around 44.30/32, bit was still hanging on to recent highs last seen at end-March. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said light exporter dollar sales around 44.35 limited losses. \par \par \uc2  They said the baht was taking its cue from the yen, with several players on the sidelines waiting for the ECB decision's impact on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Baht gains will be limited to around 44.25/28 where there could be covering of dollar shorts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was dampened after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its growth forecast for this year to 1.5-2.0 percent from a previous projection of 2-3 percent due to a slowdown in exports. \par \par \uc2  Despite the forecast downgrade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark 14-day repo rate unchanged at 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso hovered around Wednesday's close of 51.19 supported by dollar selling by three foreign banks which also raised suspicion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was behind the move. \par \par \uc2  Trading was subdued with $55.50 million traded, against $90.30 million on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not only supported the peso in recent weeks but was also buying dollars on dips to fund maturing commitments in the non-deliverable forward market. \par \par \uc2  There was a muted response to second quarter GDP data which showed growth of 3.3 percent on the year, higher than market forecasts of 2.25 percent and the government's estimate of 2.8-3.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  First quarter GDP growth was also revised up to 3.2 percent from the previous 2.5 percent. And the figures encouraged the government to keep its 2001 forecast at 3.3-3.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would need consistent improvement in economic data to alter its bearish view on the growth outlook. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won slipped slightly, as concerns over Hynix Semiconductor outweighed exporters' dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent the session wedged in a narrow 1,282.7-1,284.4 range as players wondered whether to follow the firmer yen or the losses on the local stock market, where investors were upset over a 15 percent fall in shares of debt-laden Hynix. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers noted state-run banks were spotted buying dollars around 1,284, but did not believe it was on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar nudged slightly higher, but was trapped in an increasingly narrow range of 34.572-34.587. \par \par \uc2  Since August 20, the local dollar has kept to a 34.496-34.660 range as the market remained conscious of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vigilance. The bank actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility, and has recently been spotted capping the Taiwan dollar's upside to protect the island's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said the bank was believed to be waiting around the 34.57 level during the session. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar lingered around the 1.75 mark with trade subdued ahead of the ECB decision. \par \par \uc2  The euro, yen and dollar are believed to be major components in the undisclosed trade-weighted basket Singapore uses to manage its exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Amid a lack of fresh local and regional leads, the market was expected to remain fixated on movements in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was lifted off its intraday trough of around 9,200 following suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  which was detected selling up to $25 million. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured to have unwound dollars from 9,125 to 9,075 rupiah, both directly and through brokers. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, BI kept its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in the rupiah interbank money market unchanged at 15.125 percent for the overnight rate and 15.875 percent for the seven-day rate. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Boediono said the government was considering assuming a rupiah rate of 8,000-9,000 to the dollar for next year's budget. The 2001 budget targets a rate of 9,600 rupiah. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0849 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.76       119.92         +0.13\par  Sing dlr      1.7470       1.7500         +0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    34.582       34.593         +0.03\par  Korean won   1283.50      1281.10         -0.19\par  Baht           44.29        44.23         -0.14\par  Peso           51.20        51.19         -0.02\par  Rupiah       8960.00      9090.00         +1.45\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.76       114.45         -4.43\par  Sing dlr      1.7470       1.7365         -0.60\par  Taiwan dlr    34.582       32.900         -4.86\par  Korean won   1283.50      1277.00         -0.51\par  Baht           44.29        43.70         -1.33\par  Peso           51.20        50.75         -0.88\par  Rupiah       8960.00      9470.00         +5.69\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \