\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Up On Rumored  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2001\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended stronger in thin trade Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumored to have sold dollars to boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't comment on the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Senior Economics Minister Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti said the authorities would let the market determine the rupiah's level. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed Asian trade at IDR8,925, much lower than IDR9,175 late Wednesday. The dollar moved in a IDR8,910 to IDR9,140 range. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose strongly this week on demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state oil and gas giant Pertamina to fund imports, and from local companies with foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  But rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though local banks, helped the unit in thin trade. Daily volumes in Indonesia are only around $200 million to $300 million, making it easy for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move trade if it wants to. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned the rupiah's gains since President Megawati Sukarnoputri came to power in late July might get wiped out if the flows for debt repayment continue. \par \par \uc2  In the second half of the year, some $14.7 billion in government and private foreign debt will come due, according to unofficial Bank Indonesia data. This will put pressure on the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell from its year highs around IDR12,000 when Megawati came to power last month, ending months of political pressure. \par \par \uc2  Investors are now waiting to see how successfully the government can implement asset sales promised in an agreement with the International Monetary Fund this week. \par \par \uc2  Quick sales of assets, including Bank Central Asia, would allow the government to narrow its budget deficit and reduce its reliance on foreign debt funding. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should find support at IDR8,900 Friday, with resistance at IDR9,050. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277; tom.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010830dx8u000mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
