\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 's Econ Min: Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Help Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2001\par 04:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top economics minister said Thursday the authorities won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The renewed weakness in the rupiah is temporary due to dollar demand from local private companies," Senior Economics Minister Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti told reporters before the weekly cabinet meeting. \par \par \uc2  "We aren't going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Let's leave it to market forces," he added. \par \par \uc2  Still, Jakarta-based bankers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold $10 million early Thursday to help the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help smooth movements in the rupiah but never to comment on specific actions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is trading at IDR9,100 Thursday morning, having broken through IDR9,000 resistance this week on continued foreign debt repayments from local companies. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia is keen to ensure that the rupiah doesn't lose its gains since President Megawati Sukarnoputri came to power in late July, ending months of political crisis that had sent the dollar as high as IDR12,000. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 6221 3983 1277;\par tom.wright@dowjones.com\par -0- 30/08/01 02-48G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010830dx8u0005i\par }\page {\par\f