\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets - Depressed by U.S data, Japan slides. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 1,077 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2001\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 29 (Reuters) - Asian stocks stumbled on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday as sentiment was bruised by losses in Japan's stocks \par \par \uc2  and bleak U.S. consumer confidence data which the market feared \par \par \uc2  could translate into less demand for Asia's exports. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Tokyo's key Nikkei average         marked a 17-year closing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low, shedding 1.87 percent to end at 10,979.76 after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par disappointing comments on banks' bad loans from the nation's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par top financial regulator prompted investors to sell bank stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Finance Services Minister Hakuo Yanagisawa said late on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday the outstanding balance of bad loans at major banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would likely remain near current levels through fiscal 2003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We have to remember that for the past two years the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was running on the promise of restructuring whereas very little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par change actually materialise," said Richard Jerram, chief\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economist at ING Barings Securities in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think there's still plenty more bad news out there and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as long as the government is not delivering anything\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par particularly helpful, I don't see any reason to be rushing into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market at these levels," he told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Korea, growing concerns over credit risk of Hynix\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Semiconductor knocked almost two percent off the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark KOSPI which ended at 565.63.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    GRIM ECONOMIC DATA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The markets expect a batch of fresh economic data from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par countries across the region this week, with analysts reckoning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they are likely to confirm views the worst is not over yet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korea's current account surplus fell for the second\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straight month in July as exports continued to fall, stirring\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par talk in the market the country might need another round of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rate cut.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Korea said the surplus declined by nearly half\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to a provisional $511 million in July from a revised $1.05\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion in June and a 22-month high of $2.16 billion in May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country is due to release July industrial output on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday. A Reuters' poll expected the output to drop 0.9 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the month after a U.S.-led downturn in the global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par electronics sector has hit exports from Korea.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippines will publish the second-quarter gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic product data on Thursday. Some analysts said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par number could surprise on the upside due to growth in farm and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par service sectors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "In our view, the market is focusing too much on the recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plunge in exports and discounting the resilience in both the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par agricultural and service sector," said a DBS report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Economists polled by Reuters forecast an average GDP growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 2.25 percent year-on-year in the April-June period, compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the first quarter annual growth of 2.50 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Bank of Thailand will release its monthly economic data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Friday which are likely to continue to paint a bleak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic picture of the country.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said he would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par proposed his revised 2001 economic growth forecast of 1.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent to the monetary board meeting on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But despite the economic slowdown, the government appears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to cut interest rates to spur the economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Pridiyathorn said he expected the board to leave the benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-day repo rate to be left unchanged at 2.50 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SETTLE INTO RANGE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were trapped in their recent ranges as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par impact of a weak dollar was diluted somewhat by uncertainty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the yen direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen tested the intraday low against both the euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  and the dollar after Japanese Finance Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Masajuro Shiokawa said he expected the country's April-June GDP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data to be bad.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     He said the need for a supplementary government budget to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support the economy was becoming more evident.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah slipped to the wrong side of 9,000 after recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong gains due to strong corporate demand for the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But its downside was limited by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumoured to have sold $20-30\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million directly and through brokers from 9,150.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht retained its firm tone as some players continued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to pare long dollar positions before the new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reporting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rules take effect in September 3.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said news that the monetary policy board may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par leave benchmark interest rates unchanged was likely to keep the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht's upside limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some economists believe lower interest rates will benefit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand more because it will reduce costs of the government's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stimulus programmes, given the government is likely to spend\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more to get the economy going.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0826 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \p