\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Spellbound by stagnant yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,077 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2001\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 29 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  crawled towards the higher end of their recent ranges as the yen managed to hold the 120 level. \par \par \uc2  But the market was not terribly impressed by the slight move higher as most players stood on the sidelines and waited for the dollar and yen to end their stand-off around the 120 mark. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said while the market still felt a twinge of dollar bearishness, players had become frustrated by the yen's failure to gain further ground on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  However, given the soggy sentiment surrounding the dollar, few players were willing to have a go at building long U.S. dollar positions at current levels. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah bucked the trend and headed decisively south as local corporate dollar demand kicked in. But given the thin liquidity in the market, and the restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, the rupiah market tends to set its own tone. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, investors were waiting for revised second-quarter gross domestic product data from the U.S. due later in the day. \par \par \uc2  On the domestic front, the Philippines will be issuing second-quarter GDP on Thursday and Hong Kong will release its second-quarter GDP results on Friday. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar spent most of the session hugging the 1.7500 level, up from 1.7536 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar had recovered in overnight trade in New York. But with the yen bobbing around just above 120 in Asian trade, the Sing dollar hesitated to make further advances. \par \par \uc2  "We're just playing the range right now," said a European bank dealer. He added the market was content to wait for the dollar/yen to set a decisive tone. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was swept below the 9,000 level by dollar demand from local corporates seeking to service or repay foreign debt, despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier in the day it was unhappy with the rupiah's levels, and threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. Jakarta dealers said they suspected the bank sold dollars directly in the market as well as through brokers. \par \par \uc2  But they added the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to little avail given the huge demand for dollars by Indonesia's heavily indebted firms. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah had enjoyed a brief spurt of strength thanks to optimism over the new government and the signing of a new letter of intent between Jakarta and the IMF. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts have said its rally would be short-lived given the enormity of the problems the country faces. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht gave up some of its gains after failing to break above 44.10, but it retained a firm bias on the back of dollar unwinding ahead of September 3 when new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules take effect. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also underpinned by hopes of more portfolio inflows after the government announced it would contribute to foreign funds set up to invest in the Thai market. \par \par \uc2  News the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to cut the benchmark 14-day repo rate barely supported the baht, dealers said. Some analysts believe lower rates would benefit Thailand, especially as the government needs to spend more to boost the economy. \par \par \uc2  The baht remains in a broad month-old uptrend channel against the dollar, but dealers attributed this mostly to a dollar correction rather than any improvement in baht fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs eased in the offshore market, with the one-month forward rate dropping to -5/10 satang to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at 51.19, barely changed from Tuesday's close of 51.20. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said local corporate demand for dollars emerged around the 51.15 level. But when the dollar/peso touched 51.25, a foreign bank was spotted selling around $10-$15 million, sending players out of their long dollar positions as they suspected the bank was acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the market shrugged off comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would consider further rate cuts if the peso stabilises. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura also said he would consider easing liquidity reserve requirements if peso liquidity was too tight. \par \par \uc2  The bank raised reserve requirements twice recently by a total of four percentage points to support the peso. KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won trickled back the wrong side of 1,280 per dollar after Tuesday's brief spike ran up against fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and worries about Hynix Semiconductor . \par \par \uc2  State-run Korea Development Bank said it was not considering measures to help out Hynix, a day after the troubled company said it was pulling out of a government-led debt underwriting programme, stepping up pressure on trusts to roll over its debts. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was also clouded by news Korea's current account surplus for July nearly halved to a provisional $511 million from $1.05 billion in June as exports fell faster than imports. TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar inched higher, but trade was confined to a well-worn range as players kept a wary eye on the yen and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been active in stamping out volatility in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  The mood was brightened by a sharp rebound in Taipei shares , which gained 3.2 percent after the government approved a proposal to halve the land incremental tax for two years, its first action of the over 300 recommendations made by an advisory panel at the weekend to boost the economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0858 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.92       120.37         +0.38\par  Sing dlr      1.7499       1.7536         +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.593       34.602         +0.03\par  Korean won   1281.10      1280.00         -0.09\par  Baht           44.22        44.26         +0.09\par  Peso           51.17        51.20         +0.06\par  Rupiah       9130.00      8930.00         -2.19\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.92       114.45         -4.56\par  Sing dlr      1.7499       1.7365         -0.77\par  Taiwan dlr    34.593       32.900         -4.89\par  Korean won   1281.10      1277.00         -0.32\par  Baht           44.22        43.70         -1.18\par  Peso           51.17        50.75         -0.82\par  Rupiah       9130.00      9470.00         +3.72\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010829dx8t00iu5\par }\page {\par\fs2