\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Dollar bulls brow-beaten. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2001\par 11:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 10 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were in bouncy spirits in late trade on Friday as the U.S. dollar fell to multi-month lows against both the euro and yen. \par \par \uc2  Local factors also featured strongly. The Philippine peso racked up 2.32 percent on the day following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second liquidity reserve requirement hike in three weeks. \par \par \uc2  But the yen's rise against the dollar stalled after the Japanese government's monthly report downgraded its official view of the economy for the sixth time this year. \par \par \uc2  Government pressure on the Bank of Japan to ease its monetary stance could also limit the yen's gains against the weaker dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  This would mean the upside for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which tend to track the yen closely, would also be limited in the near-term. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hit a day high of 1.7630, its best level since March 9, as gains in the yen and euro, major components in Singapore's trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , set off rounds of short-covering. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. name sold the dollar aggressively from New York trading into Friday's Asian session. Gains were exaggerated by the fact that many players in Singapore were away for a long weekend after Thursday's National Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  There was talk of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore checking rates around 1.7600, which deterred dollar sales only briefly. Players continued to pared long dollar positions after the Sing dollar broke clearly above that level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the next key level would be 1.7500 which could be broken in London or New York, barring MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the market was still long of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Friday confirmed the growth rate turned negative in the second quarter due to a sharp slowdown in electronics manufacturing. \par \par \uc2  Second quarter GDP fell 0.9 percent on-year and 10.7 percent on an annualised quarter-on-quarter basis. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was unfazed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosure rules announced late in the day as they were in line with market expectations. \par \par \uc2  It gained almost 0.50 from late Thursday levels, breaching the 45.20 mark for the first time since June 29, mostly because of the sharp rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  The rules do not require banks to identify non-residents and counterparties. Commercial banks had resisted a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  proposal to reveal names of counterparties as this would breach confidentiality laws in some countries. \par \par \uc2  But the Bank of Thailand said it would require more details on underlying reasons for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  transfers from October 1. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won kept off its early high of 1,278.5 due to fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its rise. \par \par \uc2  Rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spread when local banks were spotted buying dollars as the won broke above 1,280 for the first time since June 1, when it hit a high of 1,277.5. \par \par \uc2  But a broadly weaker dollar, higher local stocks and talk of foreign direct investment flows to Korean companies underpinned the won. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso breached the 52 mark to touch a seven-week high of 51.70 as commercial banks trimmed their dollar longs following a two percentage point hike in liquidity requirements on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said the peso was supported by export-related inflows but the upmove gathered pace when some foreign banks were seen selling dollars, sparking rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market. \par \par \uc2  Eyeing the foreign banks, usually active on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , corporates seeking dollars moved to the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday raised liquidity reserve requirements of commercial banks by two percentage points to 11 percent to mop up excess liquidity. The rise was in addition to a two percentage point hike on July 27. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar reached its highest point since Monday thanks to the firmer yen, though dealers said its gains were tempered by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said the bank had prevented the local dollar from closing above the 34.60 level in recent sessions. It has not finished beyond that point since falling sharply past 34.50 a month ago in what analysts believe was a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -engineered depreciation to boost export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  But there was little cause for cheer on the domestic front, with the overdue loan ratio at domestic banks hitting a record high of 6.47 percent at end-June from 5.89 percent at end-March. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan is due to release second quarter gross domestic product data next Friday. Economists polled by Reuters expected GDP to have contracted for the first time in 26 years due to sluggish private investment, slowing domestic consumption and sharp falls in exports. \par \par \uc2  The survey of 10 economists produced an average forecast of a 0.30 percent on-year decline in second quarter GDP after growth of 1.06 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  Verbal and rumoured actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted the rupiah to a day high of 9,090, but it failed to firm past the 9,000 level due to strong corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said BI was believed to have sold $10-15 million through state banks to capitalise on recent gains inspired by the improved political situation. \par \par \uc2  "We believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was behind the dollar sales this morning," said a dealer at a European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  "After that, corporate players were in the market to buy dollars on dips and pushed the rupiah back to 9,140 before it recouped some lost ground later in the day," said the dealer. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said the rupiah, already up more than 20 percent since a change in leadership nearly three weeks ago, could hit 8,000 per dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0916 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.08       123.48         +1.15\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.7760         +1.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.625       34.662         +0.11\par  Korean won   1280.00      1287.00         +0.55\par  Baht           45.25        45.41         +0.35\par  Peso           51.82        53.00         +2.28\par  Rupiah       9095.00      9150.00         +0.60\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f