\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Tread familiar ground as yen stalls. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,034 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Mai 2001\par 04:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 23 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were nestled comfortably in their recent ranges early Wednesday as the dollar stalled against the yen. \par \par \uc2  With expectations the yen would remain in the 120-125 per dollar range for now, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not in a hurry to go anywhere. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Asia were also looking for further clues as to where the U.S. economy was headed in the coming quarters. \par \par \uc2  While there has yet to be solid evidence of a pick-up in growth in the U.S., sentiment on Wall Street seemed to brightening, and could spill over to Asia. \par \par \uc2  Several Federal Reserve officials expressed optimism late Tuesday about the economy, predicting an increase in growth in the second half one the recent Fed cuts start kicking in. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts warned against following Wall Street's example given weaker growth, local political risks in Southeast Asia and other threats to emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  "Apart from U.S. growth continuing to be weak, there also remain key risks from the other emerging markets especially Brazil and Argentina while the political situation in Indonesia is likely to weigh on Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the next few months," Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was still shaky, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was capping the dollar's gains at 33.50. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollar/ Taiwan continued to be well-bid, especially given recent poor economic data. \par \par \uc2  Both April industrial output and export orders came in worse than expected on Tuesday at 5.85 percent and 6.6 percent on year, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the government is running out of options in spurring the economy, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent six rate cuts. They added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has little interest in seeing a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won ticked up taking its cue from a steadier yen and a firmer local bourse with stop-loss sales triggered at the open. \par \par \uc2  Singapore dealers said the Nasdaq's sixth rise in a row and continuing talks about the sale of Daewoo Motor and Hyundai Investment Trust & Securities would keep the sentiment buoyed and may limit the downside. \par \par \uc2  But they added a poor economic outlook and lingering uncertainty over recovery in the global tech sector would cap any significant gains. \par \par \uc2  They said dollar demand was expected to grow stronger around 1,285 level. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed from late New York levels of 1.8100-1.8115 on early dollar offers from local banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said given the lack of fresh domestic leads, the Sing was likely seek direction from the yen and other regionals. \par \par \uc2  The near-term downside was seen capped around 1.8120-1.8130 on lingering fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They said some interbank players were spotted buying U.S. dollars around 1.8080-1.8090 and stronger dollar bids from local corporates were likely to emerge around 1.8050-1.8060. \par \par \uc2  The April consumer price data is due later Wednesday but dealers said it may not have a huge impact unless it surprises the market. The March consumer price index rose 1.8 percent on-year, and was up 0.2 percent from February. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was resting in a well-worn range, having avoided a break of support around 45.66. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said trading was extremely thin with sporadic dollar offers from exporters supporting the baht. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the cabinet approved a finance ministry proposal to cut corporate tax for listed firms, part of a capital market stimulus package adopted by the government to help revive the bearish Thai stock market. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso opened a tad firmer at 50.60 against Tuesday's close of 50.64. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said local banks took profit on their long dollar positions as the yen edged higher. They expected players would buy the dollar on dips around 50.50. \par \par \uc2  Finance Undersecretary Juanita Amatong said late Tuesday the government planned to issue as much as $1 billion worth of bonds in the United States, Japan and Europe next month. \par \par \uc2  She said the government aimed to raise between $500 million and $700 million from the bond float and added Manila was willing to issue more if there was demand. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines' gross international reserves fell slightly to $14.44 billion at the end of April from the previous month's $14.67 billion. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was idling around the 11,400 level, trapped by local corporate dollar demand in a market heavily long on dollar. \par \par \uc2  With few solid leads in the market and Indonesia's political crisis off the boil, the rupiah has been caught between a narrow 11,075-11,560 since May 11, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said if President Abdurrahman Wahid resigns before the impeachment process is kicked off, there was a chance the rupiah could spike higher. But the likelihood of a resignation was dim. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was unable to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "too much" to help the rupiah, without elaborating. \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has $28 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves compared to Thailand's $32.1 billion aand Taiwan's $111 billion. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0233 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.11\tab  123.17\tab    +0.87\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8081\tab  1.8105\tab    +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr     33.46\tab   33.46\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1287.50\tab 1295.00\tab    +0.58\par  Baht\tab      45.53\tab   45.60\tab    +0.15\par  Peso\tab      50.40\tab   50.50\tab    +0.20\par  Rupiah\tab 11405.00     11415.00\tab    +0.09\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.11\tab  114.45\tab    -6.27\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8081\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.96\par  Taiwan dlr     33.40\tab   32.90\tab    -1.50\par  Korean won   1287.50\tab 1277.00\tab    -0.82\par  Baht\tab      45.53\tab   43.70\tab    -4.02\par  Peso\tab      50.40\tab   50.75\tab    +0.69\par  Rupiah\tab 11405.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -16.97\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5n038x0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
