\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Boosted by Wall St,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  moves. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,079 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2001\par 03:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged higher in early trade on Thursday as strong gains on Wall Street provided a psychological boost by raising hopes for more inflows. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial average rose 34.95 points or 3.15 percent to close above the key 11,000 mark for the first time since September 14. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were also reluctant to buy the dollar against some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they were unnerved by recent actions by central banks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore confirmed to a local newspaper on Wednesday that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last week to support the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Thailand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would tighten disclosure rules on baht trading for non-resident accounts from July 2 to curb speculation on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  And Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expected to keep conducting "prudent and measurable" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent excessive hikes in interest rates which are already at 21-month highs. \par \par \uc2  BI has been gradually raising rates in a largely unsuccessful attempt to stem the rupiah's losses. But critics said such moves would hurt the state budget and the troubled banking sector. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was trading around two-week highs after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would soon take more steps to stave off speculation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players rushed to pare long dollar positions, although some bargain hunting was likely to emerge below 45.20. \par \par \uc2  They said the next key target for the baht is 45.06 which it has failed to breach since April 19. \par \par \uc2  On the credit rating front, Fitch IBCA, Duff & Phelps said on Wednesday it had no plans to change Thailand's sovereign ratings and stable outlook despite the regional and global slowdown. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar climbed above 1.8100, thanks to scattered buying by interbank players early in the morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were ever more wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, given its rare confirmation that it sold the U.S. dollar last week. Finance Minister Richard Hu also spooked dealers by saying the amounts involved in recent overseas acquisitions by local companies were not large enough to move the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  That fear helped the Sing dollar clamber back to 3-= week highs, off 11-year lows of 1.8265 hit last week. \par \par \uc2  And some dealers expected further liquidation of long dollar positions after the issue of April non-oil exports data, due at 0430 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters expected on a 1.8 percent rise against a 2.1 percent contraction in March thanks to a low base effect and the weaker Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was loitering around the 11,300 level with players reluctant to trade given the country's volatile politics. \par \par \uc2  President Abdurrahman Wahid said earlier in the week he expected to be impeached, though he added that he would continue fighting and would also run for the 2004 presidential polls. His spokesman later denied he had said he expected to be impeached. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Indonesian political leaders have said an impeachment session seemed inevitable. \par \par \uc2  On the economic front, Finance Minister Prijadi Praptosuhardjo said on Wednesday the cabinet would discuss changes to the 2001 budget and submit them to parliament soon. \par \par \uc2  Those revisions were expected to be handed down to parliament in mid-May, and need to be ratified for the IMF to review Jakarta's progress on reforms and resume lending. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO The peso edged up to 50.09 against Wednesday's local 50.14 close, helped by firmer regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said energy and power companies were looking to buy the dollar at around 49.80, otherwise staying on the sidelines to wait for more attractive levels. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the prospect of a rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped lift the mood. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said the Monetary Board was biased to cut key interest rates following the U.S. rate cut. The board holds its weekly meeting later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines' overnight borrowing rate is currently at 9.5 percent and the lending rate at 11.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  A firmer yen lifted the Taiwan dollar, which ended at a six-week low of 32.957 on Wednesday, pushing it back the right side of 32.90. \par \par \uc2  The market was viewing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent dollar-buying as an effort to guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower in order to maintain Taiwan's export competitiveness amid slowing demand. \par \par \uc2  For the past few weeks, the bank has kept the local dollar in a tight range of 32.85-90, but allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to close past 32.90 for the first time since April 30 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won recovered some ground thanks to the firmer yen. \par \par \uc2  An early rally on the local bourse also lifted sentiment towards the won with the market hoping for further foreign funds' equity-linked inflows. \par \par \uc2  Even though Korean shares ended lower on Wednesday, foreign investors were net buyers, purchasing a net 16.6 billion won worth of shares. They bought a net 5.2 billion won worth of shares in early trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, the won was unable to hold onto its earlier high of 1,301.5. For the past two sessions, it has been unable to break resistance of around 1,302 convincingly as local importers sought dollars on dips. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0136 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.22\tab  123.72\tab    +0.41\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8083\tab  1.8131\tab    +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    32.945\tab  32.957\tab    +0.04\par  Korean won   1302.00\tab 1309.10\tab    +0.55\par  Baht\tab      45.19\tab   45.41\tab    +0.50\par  Peso\tab      50.07\tab   50.14\tab    +0.14\par  Rupiah\tab 11365.00     11410.00\tab    +0.40\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.22\tab  114.45\tab    -7.12\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8083\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.97\par  Taiwan dlr    32.945\tab  32.900\tab    -0.14\par  Korean won   1302.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.92\par  Baht\tab      45.19\tab   43.70\tab    -3.29\par  Peso\tab      50.07\tab   50.75\tab    +1.36\par  Rup