\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed cuts soothe some, but yen weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2001\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly firmer in late trade on Wednesday after interest rate cuts by the Federal Reserve raised hopes of economic recovery in the world's major growth locomotive. \par \par \uc2  In a statement that followed the cut, the fifth 50 basis point reduction so far this year, the Fed repeated concerns about falling investment spending and weak corporate profits. \par \par \uc2  But the positive impact of the cut was countered by a weaker yen which retraced to its two-week lows around 124 amid talk of Japanese investor demand for overseas assets. \par \par \uc2  Local factors also played a key role in lifting some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the Singapore dollar and the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar made strong gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore confirmed it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to offset the impact of strong M&A outflows. Dealers said the confirmation, which is unusual, served as a notice that it would not tolerate further slippage in its trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht lurched higher after the Bank of Thailand said it would further tighten disclosure rules on the baht to stave off speculation. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht lept above 45.40 on news the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was planning to further tighten disclosure rules on baht trading for non-resident accounts from July 2. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand spokesman Bandid Nijathaworn said financial institutions would need to give more information about spot, forward, and swap transactions, derivative transactions, equity or debt instrument deals between them and non-resident accounts. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said market participants rushed to cut losses by unwinding long dollar positions after the baht breached above 45.40, although the dollar retracement was met promptly by demand from companies and importers. \par \par \uc2  Baht funding costs in the offshore market also eased further as demand to borrow the baht to fund dollar holdings ebbed. The one-month forward rate was quoted at 9.5/17.0 satang per dollar, but there was not much trade done as the spread was wide. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed as local banks offloaded U.S. dollars following comments from authorities reaffirming their commitment to a tightening monetary bias. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore confirmed, in the local press, it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to offset the impact of an M&A inspired hike in corporate demand for the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Richard Hu told parliament the amounts involved in recent overseas acquisitions by local companies were not large enough to move the Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks led the U.S. dollar sales and were followed by players already seeking to trim long positions. \par \par \uc2  "The near-term trading range could be 1.8100-1.8140 but that is contingent to the yen not weakening significantly beyond 124," a chief dealer of a European bank in Singapore said. INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah hovered around 11,400 with the market eyeing warily President Aburrahman Wahid's comment that he would not quit and would in fact fight the next presidential polls in 2004. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Wahid told a seminar he expected to be impeached by parliament but on Wednesday his spokesman denied he made the comment. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said trading conditions were thin with most activity led by state banks active on both sides of the market. \par \par \uc2  However, most players kept to the sidelines as heads of parliamentary factions met to discuss a possible change in leadership and timing of any impeachment hearing against Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah and avoid excessive hike in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the Fed rate cut could have an impact on its weekly SBI certificate auction, which saw the one-month rate reach 16.31 percent from 16.26 percent last week. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won edged lower in line with the falling yen, touching a two-week low of 1,310.2, where some export and equity-related inflows capped the downside. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said hopes of foreign direct investment inflows from the potential sale of Daewoo Motor Co. and Hynix Semiconductor to foreign investors kept sentiment supported. \par \par \uc2  The consumer confidence survey for April also came in better than the previous month but dealers in Singapore said they were more worried about the economy of Korea's biggest export market. \par \par \uc2  With a recovery in the U.S. still unclear despite the Fed's aggressive rate cuts, the won was expected to stay depressed. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ended at 50.14 after reaching a high of 50.06 from lows of 50.21. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said local banks bought the peso earlier, but foreign banks and IT companies were looking to buy the U.S. dollar at 50.10-20. \par \par \uc2  The government said the preliminary January-April budget deficit was 36.717 billion pesos, lower than its target of 38.3 billion for the period. \par \par \uc2  President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo said the Philippines was aiming to bring down its budget deficit to 130-145 billion pesos this year from its initial estimate of 225 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the government needs to consolidate its chronic deficit urgently, otherwise it would inflict more damage on the economy given that total public sector debt is approaching 80 percent of GDP. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would consider the inflation trend in deciding whether to lower its overnight rates following the U.S. rate cut. The overnight borrowing rate is currently at 9.5 percent and the lending rate at 11.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to six-week troughs of 32.996, tracking the yen lower. Dealers said U.S. investment houses bought the dollar following the TAIEX's poor showing. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cut its interest rates, following the Fed's move on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut key interest rates by 0.125 percentage points, bringing the discount rate to 4.0 percent and the collateral rate to 4.375 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0854 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.68\tab  123.27\tab    -0.33\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8125\tab  1.8182\tab    +0.31\par  Taiwan dlr    32.957\tab  32.930\tab    -0.08\par  Korean won   1309.10\tab 1303.20\tab    -0.45\par  Baht\tab      45.37\tab   45.50\tab    +0.29\par  Peso\tab      50.11\tab   50.18\tab    +0.14\par  Rupiah\tab 11410.00     11460.00\tab    +0.44\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f