\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah falls past 12,000,others wary. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2001\par 03:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 26 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah toppled over the key 12,000 mark early Thursday, threatening to ruffle other Southeast Asian markets. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah's slide past 12,000 per dollar was prompted by increasing jitters over the country's messy economic and political scene. Among the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  most vulnerable to shocks from the rupiah were the neighbouring Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Emerging markets in Asia were also vulnerable to the latest events in Argentina, where rumours continue to circulate about a debt default and a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The latter took a step towards reality when Argentina's President Fernando de la Rua earlier named an interim head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The current \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Pedro Pou had come under increasing fire for refusing to ease strict monetary policies, including the Argentine peso's one-to-one peg. \par \par \uc2  On the bright side, U.S. data issued on Wednesday showed the key housing sector surprisingly resilient and helped dispel some of the gloom over the U.S. economy's prospects. That data fed into a more upbeat mood on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  The yen was treading water as the market waited for the new Japanese cabinet line-up, while the euro was also stuck with investors keeping watch over the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  With the fate of international loans in the air, Jakarta has been scrambling to fill in its budget shortfall, usually papered over by loans from international lenders. \par \par \uc2  The government announced on Wednesday that it would issue its first ever rupiah deficit bonds, with the expectation that wealthy local governments would buy them. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, said the move was cosmetic and did not address the main cause of Indonesia's budget shortfall - an unwillingness to cut expenditures, namely costly fuel subsidies. \par \par \uc2  Markets in Jakarta were also girding themselves for a potentially violent showdown between embattled President Abdurrahman Wahid's supporters and opponents. \par \par \uc2  Parliament is widely expected to issue a second censure of Wahid over two financial scandals, which may spark violent protests from his more fanatical supporters. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was trapped in a narrow range of 45.50-45.70 in subdued trade. Dealers expected the dollar's upside to be limited as the market was already quite long. \par \par \uc2  Players were also reluctant to actively bid for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they were wary of further tightening of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading regulations. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chettavee Chareonpitak told Reuters in Bangkok that the Bank of Thailand was making an internal study on whether to tighten reporting requirements to help it monitor and curb speculation on the baht by non-residents with access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are looking at additional reporting on non-resident baht accounts, such as information on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion by accounts owners," he said. \par \par \uc2  Charts show dollar/baht confined in a consolidative triangle which could break any time soon. \par \par \uc2  "I think people will be taking profits on the dollar in the near-term because the market is quite long. That should prepare the dollar for another rally," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was cowering at 1.8160 after an offshore rout knocked it down to two-week lows of 1.8180 from 1.8100. \par \par \uc2  Underlying weakness stemmed from murky regional political picture, anticipation for further M&A-related flows and little improvements on economic fundamentals, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local banks, U.S. investment banks were covering its short U.S. dollar positions, but the Sing dollar's fall came to a halt at 1.8180, level where the authorities were said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a decisive break of 1.8180 would lead to stop-loss U.S. dollar buying orders at 1.8200 then 1.8225, risking a return to decade lows of 1.8235 hit on April 2. \par \par \uc2  March manufacturing output is due out later on Thursday. In February it rose 13.3 percent but analysts anticipate weakness ahead given a downturn in the global technology sector. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won made slight gains with the help of the steady yen, but its rise was capped by importers seeking dollars. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen remained the main driver of the won's direction as Korea and Japan compete on a number of key exports. They added, however, month-end exporters' dollar sales may serve to give the won a short-term boost. \par \par \uc2  The market was keeping watch over March industrial output numbers due at 0300 GMT. A recent Reuters poll showed economists on average expected a 0.2 percent decline on month, mainly due to sluggish electronics exports. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso opened a touch weaker at 50.60 in the onshore market, compared with the Wednesday's close of 50.55, with interbank players and importers bidding for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the arrest of former president Joseph Estrada had limited impact on the market, although some said lack of mass support for him was good for political stability. \par \par \uc2  "The market is closely watching the regionals and developments in Argentina for direction," said a Manila dealer. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the peso would poke above 50.40 in the near-term because that is where lots of people are going to buy the dollar on dips," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market drew little support from Finance Secretary Alberto Romulo's remark, saying this year's budget deficit could be at 132 billion pesos, lower than the government's official target of 145 billion. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR The Taiwan dollar ticked up to 32.87 from 32.90 late on Thursday but was expected to come under pressure given weaker regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading would remain lucklustre with offshore players looking to square positions ahead of Japan's Golden Week Holiday which starts this weekend. \par \par \uc2  They also said exporters were likely to come in to sell the U.S. dollar at around 32.95, and equity-related capital inflows would support 33 mark, with the benchmark TAIEX up 0.5 percent after the overnight gains on the Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2  The market showed no immediate reaction to U.S. President George W. Bush reaffirming the U.S. policy on Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  He told Reuters the United States would help Taiwan defend itself against China but said he hoped Taipei and Beijing will resolve their differences peacefully. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0148 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.08\tab  122.46\tab    +0.31\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8178\tab  1.8155\tab    -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr     32.91\tab   32.91\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1295.00\tab 1307.70\tab    +0.98\par  Baht\tab      45.60\tab   45.58\tab    -0.04\par  Peso\tab      50.67\tab   50.50\tab    -0.34\par  Rupiah\tab 12050.00     11880.00\tab    -1.41\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.08\tab  114.45\tab    -6.25\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8178\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.47\par  Taiwan dlr     32.86\tab   32.90\tab    +0.12\par  Korean won   1295.00\tab 1277.00\tab    -1.39\par  Baht\tab      45.60\tab   43.70\tab    -4.17\par  Peso\tab      50.67\tab   50.75\tab    +0.16\par  Rupiah\tab 12050.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -21.41\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4q01dse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
