\par\par \b \uc2  State banks support rupiah, peso dips on Moody's. \b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2001\par 07:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0455 GMT - The Indonesian rupiah fluctuated in a wide 11,700-11,900 band with state bank dollar sales capping the downside in a thin market characterised by wide spreads. \par \par \uc2  - Jakarta dealers spotted state banks selling an estimated $20 million early, prompting unwinding of dollar longs. Action believed to be on behalf of Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denies \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  - BI says "obvious" that interest rates, already at 21-month highs, will be hiked further to help rupiah. Benchmark one-month SBI rate now at 15.93 percent. \par \par \uc2  - Market also cautious as donors under Consultative Group for Indonesia start two-day economic review meeting in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  - But dealers see rupiah upside limited by worries over expected stormy parliament session starting April 30. Corporate dollar bids seen in 11,500-11,600 range. \par \par \uc2  - Parliament likely to issue second censure motion against President Abdurrahman Wahid on alleged graft scandals and debate revised budgetary targets unveiled last week. \par \par \uc2  - Fears of violence as Indonesia's largest Muslim organisation plans to hold prayer gathering in support of Wahid on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - Thin trading in offshore non-deliverable forwards with longer dates marked up on bearish rupiah outlook. One-month NDFs quoted at 11,700.0/12,000.0 and six-month at 12,500.0/13,000.0. \par \par \uc2  - Philippine peso off early low of 50.52 touched after Moody's said ratings outlook under pressure from political uncertainty, declining economic fundamentals and worsening regional economic conditions. \par \par \uc2  - Moody's outlook for Philippines foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  country ceilings, last changed in October, stays at negative as report only annual update of market and not formal rating action. \par \par \uc2  - Manila dealers say exporter dollar sales helped peso off early low but see pressure as importers building dollar longs ahead of import season. \par \par \uc2  - Taiwan dollar hugs 32.90 on poor economic data and weak local stock market. \par \par \uc2  - March export orders fell 1.12 percent from year-ago, industrial output fell 4.38 percent and unemployment rate up to 3.89 percent from 3.73 percent in February. \par \par \uc2  - Singapore dealers said export orders and industrial output not as bad as expected but still enough to dampen sentiment. \par \par \uc2  - Taiwan official says unemployment rate expected to hit record high for second consecutive year at above 3.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  - Dealers see Taiwan dollar in 32.88-32.92 range with players fearing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4n01mp0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
