\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Buoyed by Fed cut, but rupiah suffers. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were buoyed on Thursday by the U.S. Federal Reserve's surprise rate cut overnight, raising hopes that the U.S. growth engine will keep ticking over. \par \par \uc2  A firmer yen and the Nasdaq's overnight rally also helped the regionals distance themselves from recent lows. \par \par \uc2  As expected, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  matched the Fed's 50 basis-point rate cuts at its policy-setting meeting. \par \par \uc2  But Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not immediately follow the Fed's suit, while the Bank of Thailand was not expected to cut rates at its meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  And the rupiah continued to suffer from a gloomy political outlook. Despite Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it slipped through the key psychological 11,000 mark. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Fed's decision to lower its federal funds rate to 4.5 percent, the lowest since 4.25 percent in May 1994, may help the regionals in the short term. \par \par \uc2  But the Fed's sudden move also raised concerns over the depth of the U.S. downturn that necessitated the second round inter-meeting cuts so far this year. \par \par \uc2  The yen poked above 122 and the euro was firm at three-week highs against the dollar as the market digested the Fed's move. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht rose to an intraday high of 45.07, its best level since April 2, on the back of the Fed's rate cuts and a steadier yen before onshore dollar demand set it back. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said local banks bought dollar actively above 45.10 for customers and importers. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the baht would move beyond or stand convincingly above 45.00 in the immediate term because commercial demand for the dollar is still quite strong," said a dealer at a European bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand's monetary policy board is expected to keep its key 14-day repo unchanged at 1.5 percent at its meeting later Thursday despite the Fed's cuts. \par \par \uc2  Offshore baht funding costs eased, with the one-month forward rate quoted at -3.00/-0.00 satang per dollar. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won leapt with the firmer yen and rallying local stocks, climbing above the 1,300 per dollar level for the first time since March 21. But it failed to hold onto earlier, more impressive gains. \par \par \uc2  Local stocks closed 4.23 percent higher on the back of the Fed's rate cuts and the Nasdaq's overnight gains. Foreign investors bought a net 671.6 billion won in shares, their largest net purchase since March 3, 2000. \par \par \uc2  But dealers in Singapore said the dollar was well-bid after selling by U.S. funds brought the dollar to a low of 1,293.5. \par \par \uc2  Local importers bought dollars around that level, spurring local banks to cover their dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were unsure as to how long the won would be able to hold onto its gains, given the slowing Korean economy. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The ailing rupiah sank below the 11,000 level for the first time in five weeks due to immense dollar demand from local banks and companies. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia was spotted selling dollars when the rupiah slipped to 11,035, with the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated around $15-20 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a similar amount of dollars on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  BI also threatened to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost around four percent in one week. \par \par \uc2  But dealers doubted if its persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - both through direct dollar sales and money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - would turn around the rupiah's course in the face of persistent political and economic woes. \par \par \uc2  The market has become increasingly nervous about potential violence in Jakarta ahead of April 30 when parliament is expected to issue a second censure of President Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  Wahid earlier reminded parliament of his support, saying thousands of his backers were ready to come to the capital. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar edged higher to just above 1.80 from Wednesday's lows of 1.8085, thanks to the firmer yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers emphasised the volume was thin with little genuine demand for the Sing. Many dealers said the Sing owed its rise to profit-taking on dollars. \par \par \uc2  The market did not react much to comments by Deputy Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore would maintain its monetary policy of a gently appreciating band for the Sing on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  "His comment could be an indication from the MAS that it will not change its monetary policy no matter what the Fed does," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. "That's a valid arguement and helps the MAS maintain its credibility." \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, dealers said Singapore would not be immune to the regional and U.S. slowdowns, furthering the case for a lower Sing dollar. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso firmed to a day's high of 49.96, but later trimmed its gains to stay below 50. \par \par \uc2  Manufacturers and other importers were buying dollars to meet their requirements for April and May, which is the import season. \par \par \uc2  The Phillipine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the Fed and cut its benchmark overnight borrowing and lending rates by 50 basis points, bringing them to 9.5 percent and 11.75 percent, respectively. \par \par \uc2  Dealers welcomed the move as an effort to spur domestic demand, but noted that the Philippine economy would still suffer if the U.S. slowdown lingers. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose in line with the yen, with rises in local stocks also boosting sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, it failed to hold onto its intraday high of 32.785, with the market speculating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would come in to stem the local dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in the market recently to cap its currrency's rise in order to maintain Taiwan's export competiveness. \par \par \uc2  The bank said earlier in the day it would not immediately follow the Fed's rate cuts. Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last cut rates on March 30. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0858 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.80\tab  122.95\tab    +0.94\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8008\tab  1.8054\tab    +0.26\par  Taiwan dlr     32.90\tab   32.92\tab    +0.06\par  Korean won   1298.30\tab 1313.60\tab    +1.18\par  Baht\tab      45.16\tab   45.37\tab    +0.47\par  Peso\t