\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah falls past 11,000, at 5-week low. \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 05:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 19 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slipped through the 11,000 per dollar level for the first time in five weeks in the face of heavy corporate demand for dollars, dealers in Jakarta said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  It fell to 11,005 against 10,915 late Wednesday, bringing its losses for the week to 4.21 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said companies and local banks actively bid for the dollar from 10,930 to settle import bills and to repay foreign debts due to fears the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could drop further. \par \par \uc2  "Political tensions have risen, with spats between President Abdurrahman Wahid and the parliament appearing to escalate," said a dealer at one European bank in Jakarta. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Indonesia was in the market on Wednesday to prop up the rupiah by selling around $10-15 million, but that merely slowed its slide. \par \par \uc2  They added that the bank had not been spotted in the market so far in trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In an effort to discourage further selling, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed to stem the rupiah's fall and might raise rates on its benchmark certificates (SBIs) later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The one-month SBI rate rose to 15.93 percent at Wednesday's auction from 15.82 percent the previous week. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah last breached 11,000 on March 12, when it hit a low of 11,210 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had limited ability to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4j01ntf\par }