\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesia Rupiah Ends Lower, Clouded By Domestic Politics \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 11:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah ended at a five-week low Thursday as the market grew increasingly nervous ahead of a parliamentary session on April 30, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Parliament is expected to issue a second censure to President Abdurrahman Wahid that day, moving another step closer to impeaching the president who rose to power in October 1999. \par \par \uc2  After touching an intraday high of IDR11,105, the dollar closed at IDR11,095, up from IDR10,960 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had failed to break the key psychological level of IDR11,000 earlier in the day, but Wahid's statement that 400,000 followers were ready to fight on his behalf if parliament impeaches him fueled panic dollar buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The statement made the market more nervous," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "Wahid's statement didn't do any good for the rupiah at all." \par \par \uc2  During the day, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah by selling an estimated $40 million. \par \par \uc2  But the market continued defying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , knowing the bank's limited capabilities. Bank Indonesia has only around $28 billion in gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is getting more disillusioned with prospects for the disbursement of the International Monetary Fund's next loan to Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  An IMF mission is in Jakarta to complete a review of Indonesia's economic program, but it's still unclear when it will release the $400 million installment. \par \par \uc2  In a move to tighten the supply of the rupiah that could be used to buy the dollar, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday also raised the money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, Indonesian share prices fell 1.9% to a 29-month low partly due to the rupiah's sustained fall. \par \par \uc2  After successfully maintain its close above IDR11,000, the dollar is expected to test IDR11,300 Friday, dealers said. Meanwhile, the IDR11,000 is expected to serve as a solid support for the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277 I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4j01pkk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
