\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Gov:To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2 , Hike Rates To Aid Rupiah \b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 07:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars and raising interest rates to defend the rupiah, which fell to a five-week low Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "But, what is more important to help the rupiah is that the government must implement the International Monetary Fund's economic programs and improve political situations," Sjahril told journalists. \par \par \uc2  His comment came after Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the rupiah earlier Thursday, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  But so far its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to drag the dollar to below the important pyschological level of IDR11,000. The U.S. unit was traded at IDR11,010 at 0600 GMT (2:00 a.m. EDT) as local companies were buying the dollar on concerns over rising political tension. \par \par \uc2  -By I Made Sentana,Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par -0- 19/04/01 06-12G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4j01p6f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
