\par\par \b \uc2  Bk Indonesia Raises Money Mkt Rates 50 BPs \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2001\par 04:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday raised its money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by 50-basis points for all maturities between one-day and one week. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia said the overnight rate is now 13.125%, the rates for maturities between two to six days are 13.375% and the one-week rate is 13.875%. \par \par \uc2  The rate hike follows an increase in the benchmark weighted average rate of the one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia notes to 15.93% Wednesday from 15.82%. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia has been raising rates to defend the rupiah, which is clouded by the country's bleak political outlook. \par \par \uc2  Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are the rates it offers to banks if they put their funds with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The higher rates are expected to tighten liquidity, which can be used to speculate against the rupiah in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277,\par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par -0- 19/04/01 02-25G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4j01oyc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
