\par\par \b \uc2  Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Intervenes \highlight\uc2 ,Sells Dlr To Help Rupiah-Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2001\par 03:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- Bank Indonesia sold U.S. dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early Wednesday to help the rupiah, after it was earlier traded in the local spot market at close to IDR11,000 to the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they believe Bank Indonesia sold around $10 million, but said that failed to drive the dollar significantly lower as the amount was insignificant. \par \par \uc2  Separately Bank Indonesia Governor Sjahril Sabirin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the rupiah if necessary. He, however, didn't mention anything regarding its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was traded at IDR10,965 at 0152 GMT (9:52 p.m. EDT), up from its close at IDR10,865 Tuesday as some banks cut their dollar short positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said some local companies were bidding for the U.S. unit on concerns over rising political tension. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277,\par I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com\par -0- 18/04/01 02-11G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4i01qax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
