\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier in holiday-thinned trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2001\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier late on Monday, but activity was confined to familiar range as holidays in several centres kept interest thin and volumes low. \par \par \uc2  Most Asian markets reopened after a three-day break but Hong Kong, Sydney and much of Europe were still closed for the Easter break. Thai markets were also still shut for Songkran. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expected volumes to pick up from Tuesday, but the overall trend remained unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Until the market is convinced that risk of the yen falling to much weaker levels is over, most players in the region will prefer to stay long of dollars," a chief dealer of a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Japan competes with key Asian countries in export markets and also absorbs a chunk of the region's exports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the release of poor economic data in line with the expected slowing of exports and growth across the region was also likely to keep sentiment depressed. \par \par \uc2  Singapore is due to release March non-oil domestic exports data on Tuesday after lowering its growth forecast for the year last week. Most analysts expect exports to contract after a 5.4 percent rise in February. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's downgrade of its view of the economy in its April report had little impact on the yen as the view had been widely expected. \par \par \uc2  Both the yen and euro were also rangebound in a holiday-thinned market with the dollar getting some marginal support from tension in the Middle East after Israel's air raid on Syrian positions in Lebanon earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah led regional loosers on Monday as dollar sales by state banks were badly upstaged by strong corporate demand. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said state banks sold around $10-15 million but that was not enough to halt the rupiah's slide. \par \par \uc2  One oil company was heard placing a big dollar buying order while foreign banks were also active in bidding for the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  Optimism over a potentially positive outcome from the IMF visit was overshadowed by news of the World Bank scrapping a $300 million loan to the country, partly due to its failure to meet certain requirements. \par \par \uc2  "Now the market hopes that the IMF visit would lead to the disbursement of its loans for the sake of other creditors' confidence in Indonesia. The country's public-debt profile is in virtual default," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. Meanwhile, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its indicative \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in the rupiah interbank money market unchanged at 12.625 percent for the overnight rate and 13.375 percent for the seven-day rate. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are among the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tools to influence liquidity in the market. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso was stuck in a tight range just beyond the 50 mark, with regional weakness keeping the dollar well bid while a lack of corporate dollar demand capped the downside. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said with a holiday in Bangkok and lack of a clear signal from the yen, most corporates preferred to stay on the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said key policy rates were likely to stay unchanged until the release of inflation data on May 5 and the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting on May 15. \par \par \uc2  The bank's overnight borrowing rate is currently at 10.0 percent while the overnight lending rate is at 12.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht came off its lows in late trade after being wedged in a tight range for the whole session as the onshore market was closed for the four-day Songkran holiday. Trading will resume on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar retained its bid tone, although market participants were reluctant to push or mark it up too high against the baht, fearing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest disclosure requirements would further dent dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that from May 1, banks will have to provide details on foreign debt exposure and repayment obligations when their clients buy dollars from them. \par \par \uc2  The one-month offshore forward rate was quoted at 10/15 satang per dollar while the onshore rate was quoted at -9.9/-9.0 satang. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won held off its lows as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support and possible equity-linked fund inflows limited the downside, but the soft yen left players keen to buy the dollar on dips. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors remained net buyers of Korean shares on Monday, picking up a net 1.3 billion won worth, but their purchases were well below Friday's 69.1 billion won as the Easter holiday and expectations of a softer Nasdaq dampened interest. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of direct or indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, but the market remained on guard after the authorities' recent aggressive efforts to curb the won's fall. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Monday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $93.64 billion on April 15 from $94.44 billion at end-March, partly due to a $300 million repayment to the IMF. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined comment on whether the drop in reserves was also due to recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers estimate at around $700-$800 billion. \par \par \uc2  On the economic front, the seasonally adjusted jobless rate held steady at 4.2 percent in March and analysts said it could stay above four percent for the year as the economy slows and corporate restructuring continues. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar was overshadowed by lingering pessimism over the yen and expectations of poor trade data, due on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analyst forecasts for the March data ranged from marginal gains to a contraction, with a Reuters poll producing an average forecast of a 2.87 percent on-year drop in non-oil domestic exports after February's nominal 5.4 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overall the market still favoured the U.S. dollar, but it was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier this month it was sticking to a tightening bias. \par \par \uc2  The impact of $5.8 billion DBS-Dao Heng acquisition deal ran out of steam as the market awaited further developments. One dealer said DBS had bought dollars actively in the past few weeks, indicating it might have already covered most of the cash required for the planned takeover. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar nudged lower in line with the yen and won but dealers in Singapore said fears of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was believed to be active in early trade kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its recent tight range. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 32.95 was not aggressive but was enough to signal its intention. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank in Singapore said the Taiwan dollar was unlikely to break the 32.88-32.98 range in the near term unless the yen made a major move. \par \par \uc2  A lower finish on the local stock market and last week's downgrade of the trade outlook kept sentiment depressed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0836 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.55\tab  124.15\tab    -0.32\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8073\tab  1.8050\tab    -0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    32.931\tab  32.908\tab    -0.07\par  Korean won   1329.10\tab 1325.00\tab    -0.31\par  Baht\tab      45.55\tab   45.32\tab    -0.50\par  Peso\tab      50.20\tab   49.70\tab    -1.00\par  Rupiah\tab 10765.00     10600.00\tab    -1.53\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.55\tab  114.45\tab    -8.11\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8073\tab  1.7365\tab    -3.92\par  Taiwan dlr    32.931\tab  32.900\tab    -0.09\par  Korean won   1329.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -3.92\par  Baht\tab      45.55\tab   43.70\tab    -4.06\par  Peso\tab      50.20\tab   50.75\tab    +1.10\par  Rupiah\tab 10765.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -12.03\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4g0229p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
