\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yen weighs,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  fears help. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2001\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 6 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under renewed pressure on Friday as the yen's three-day winning streak against the dollar ran into some resistance. \par \par \uc2  The yen stumbled as a much-awaited economic package by the Japanese ruling coalition failed to impress the market, but renewed jawboning boosted it in late trade. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry's Haruhiko Kuroda said it was hard to justify recent moves in the dollar/yen as there had been no big change in Japan's fundamentals and that Japan would take action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if current trends continued. \par \par \uc2  Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened higher on the back of the yen's overnight gains but a reversal of those gains sparked covering of short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  But central banks in Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the fear of that in Singapore kept the won, rupiah and Sing dollar off recent lows. \par \par \uc2  With Bangkok closed for a holiday, the baht was not so lucky and slipped to a fresh 37-month low in offshore trade. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats and actions could temporarily ease some pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the outlook remained weak on slowing growth and exports. \par \par \uc2  Fresh trading cues were likely to emerge from the U.S. March employment report due at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters on average expect a higher unemployment rate, up to 4.3 percent from February's 4.2 percent. They also forecast 58,000 new jobs were created outside the farm sector in March, compared with 135,000 in February. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR The Sing dollar kept a soft tone as the yen eased. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said local banks placed sizeable U.S. dollar orders in the afternoon, which pushed it down to session lows of 1.8184. \par \par \uc2  But the market turned wary as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was suspected to have defended that level late on Wednesday. This allowed the Sing dollar to avoid a damaging break of 1.8200 which would expose it to decade lows of 1.8230 hit on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But the market saw no signs of aggressive action by the authorities, which again spurred speculation the MAS had already shifted its monetary stance to neutral from a tightening bias. \par \par \uc2  The MAS has said it would review its monetary policy in the middle of the year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would focus on a revised growth forecast for 2001 and preliminary growth figures for the first quarter due for release on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The government estimates the economy will grow between five to seven percent this year, but economists suspect worsening external conditions could slow growth to as low as 4.8 percent. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  Offshore players took advantage of a holiday in Bangkok to push the baht to a 37-month low of 45.72. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the dollar crawled higher in ultra-thin trade, which exaggerated the impact of relatively small deals. They added U.S. names were spotted buying up dollar/baht when the yen fell past 125. \par \par \uc2  "With Bangkok on holiday, that means no Bank of Thailand. So you might as well take adventage of that," said a dealer at a European bank, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the baht earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/baht had wandered deeply into overbought territory with a reading of 84.863 on the 14-day relative strength index. \par \par \uc2  Offshore baht funding costs were still firm at 41/52 satang per dollar against 40/50 satang late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -02 \par \par \uc2  The won was propped up by the Bank of Korea as it tried to track the yen's retreat against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had directly sold about $150-200 million at around 1,358 won in late morning trade, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Both times the won rose to around its session high of 1,339.9 where importers and offshore players were seen buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which came after weeks of verbal threats and recent state bank dollar sales, was not as aggressive as expected, given the $1.5 billion average daily turnover in the won market. \par \par \uc2  They said fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably testing the depth of the market and might come in more strongly later, kept players cautious. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was firmer, but did not venture very far from Thursday's close of 32.979 as the yen wavered. \par \par \uc2  For the past several weeks, the Taiwan dollar has been tracking the yen closely as Taiwan and Japan compete on electronics exports. \par \par \uc2  Consumer inflation data showed a slight 0.44 percent on-year rise in March against February's 1.02 percent fall. Analysts said the slight rise meant inflation was still benign and may provide more room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates. \par \par \uc2  On the Taiwan dollar NDF market, the six-month rate was at 0.560/610 and the one-year was at 0.850/900. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah dipped to a near four-week low of 10,930 as early dollar buying by some state and foreign banks sent local corporates scrambling for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pumped in around $10-30 million from around 10,930 all the way to 10,850, but they added that local corporate demand for dollars was strong in the 10,750-10,800 range. \par \par \uc2  The market was unimpressed by news an IMF review mission would start its work in Jakarta on Wednesday as conditions of the visit had been met. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was likely to wait for a formal resumption of IMF lending before pushing the rupiah higher. \par \par \uc2  However, Bank Indonesia governor Sjahril Sabirin said he expected the IMF visit to help boost sentiment in the rupiah which could give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to lower interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The mission's visit should pave the way for a new $400 million loan from the IMF which has been delayed since late last year due to a dispute between Jakarta and the Fund over key reforms. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso ended at 50.200, slightly below its Thursday close after hitting a session low of 50.50 in line with weakness in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said oil importers and some foreign banks were seen bidding the dollar up in early trade but inflows from overseas workers ahead of a long weekend capped the peso's downside. \par \par \uc2  Manila's financial markets will be closed on Monday for the Day of Valour. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0907 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.68\tab  123.98\tab    -0.56\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8150\tab  1.8065\tab    -0.47\par  Taiwan dlr    32.940\tab  32.979\tab    +0.12\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1347.00\tab    +0.37\par  Baht\tab      45.58\tab   45.25\tab    -0.72\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.10\tab    +0.20\par  Rupiah\tab 10750.00     10680.00\tab    -0.65\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.68\tab  114.45\tab    -8.21\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.8150\tab  1.7365\tab    -4.33\par  Taiwan dlr    32.940\tab  32.900\tab    -0.12\par  Korean won   1342.10\tab 1277.00\tab    -4.85\par  Baht\tab      45.58\tab   43.70\tab    -4.12\par  Peso\tab      50.00\tab   50.75\tab    +1.50\par  Rupiah\tab 10750.00\tab 9470.00\tab   -11.91\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4602l3y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
