\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Dn;Off Lows On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2001\par 11:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA -(Dow Jones)- The Indonesian rupiah closed down Friday amid corporate dollar buying, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended off its earlier lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed in Asian trading at IDR10,875, off an earlier high of IDR10,940, but up from IDR10,740 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to an intraday high on buying by local companies needing to repay foreign debt, traders said. Other investors used this upward trend to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  Many investors fear the dollar will soon move through resistance at IDR11,000 amid Indonesia's political problems. \par \par \uc2  A standoff between President Abdurrahman Wahid and his political opponents in parliament is keeping foreign investors out of the market, and threatening to hurt Indonesia's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  News that the International Monetary Fund will send a mission to Jakarta Wednesday to try and kick-start the country's stalled $5 billion lending program failed to lift the rupiah. \par \par \uc2  It remains unclear whether the IMF will be able to reach agreement with Indonesia over a number of economic reforms, which the country has so far failed to implement. Chief among these is IMF concern over Jakarta's proposals to amend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  law to allow the government to fire and hire the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. \par \par \uc2  Still, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was able to pull the dollar back from its highs, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $20 million directly and another $30 million through state banks, traders said. This prompted investors to take profits on long dollar positions that had benefited from the rise in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to stop the continued downward\par trend in the rupiah, analysts say.\par -0- 06/04/01 09-06G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1159 1848 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4601jgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
