\par\par \b \uc2  Rupiah to get worse without  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2001\par 04:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JAKARTA, April 4 (Reuters) - Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the ailing rupiah, added the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would get worse without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , (the rupiah) will clearly get worse," Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Asked if that meant the bank would continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite some criticism that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had done little to stem the rupiah's fall, Sabirin said: "Yes." \par \par \uc2  Sabirin also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had so far no plan to ease rules requiring commercial banks to achieve a minimum of eight percent capital adequacy ratio (CAR) and a maximum of five percent non-performing loans (NPLs) by year-end. \par \par \uc2  Bankers and analysts had expressed concerns the weak rupiah and high interest rates would hit bank earnings, raise non-performing loan levels and eventually erode their fragile capital base, making it more difficult to meet the requirements. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4402oxm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
