\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Mixed as domestic factors rule sentiment. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jennifer Chen \par \uc2 935 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 11:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 28 (Reuters) - Asian share markets were \par \par \uc2  mixed on Wednesday with domestic factors overtaking an earlier \par \par \uc2  upbeat mood stemming from improving U.S. consumer confidence, \par \par \uc2  while \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sat tight and waited for fresh cues. \par \par \uc2      The U.S. Conference Board's consumer confidence index rose \par \par \uc2  in March, beating analysts' forecast for a fall. \par \par \uc2      The data caught most the market by surprise, driving U.S. \par \par \uc2  equities higher and fueling hopes that Asian exports might not \par \par \uc2  see a severe drop-off in demand. \par \par \uc2      However, domestic concerns hit Taiwan and Korea in \par \par \uc2  particular. Investors in Korea fretted over an expected debt \par \par \uc2  write-off for Hyundai Engineering and Construction, pushing the \par \par \uc2  benchmark Korea Composite Index lower. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over the general health of Taiwan's economy and a \par \par \uc2  disappointing dividend payment by United Microelectronics Corp \par \par \uc2  sent Taiwan shares lower. \par \par \uc2  But Tokyo share prices firmed slightly on the back of \par \par \uc2  cautious optimism that the Japanese government will muster \par \par \uc2  together policies to help the economy. \par \par \uc2  Talk that foreign investors were increasing their exposure \par \par \uc2  to Japanese equities bolstered the yen as well, \par \par \uc2  providing underlying support to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market was also speculating that the Bank of Japan's \par \par \uc2  keenly watched tankan survey of business sentiment, due on \par \par \uc2  Monday, may be better than expected. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong's Hang Seng also climbed, led by gains in China \par \par \uc2  Mobile and HSBC. \par \par \uc2      ARBITRAGE TALK ROCKS SING DOLLAR \par \par \uc2      While the steady yen kept the dollar reasonably tame \par \par \uc2  against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not able to \par \par \uc2  get close to their resistance levels. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar slipped to a low of 1.7955, its lowest \par \par \uc2  level since August 31, 1998, a few days after Singapore \par \par \uc2  Telecommunications Ltd announced its successful bid to buy \par \par \uc2  Australia's Cable & Wireless Optus. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the Sing dollar sank as hedge funds sought to \par \par \uc2  arbitrage between the shares of SingTel and Optus. \par \par \uc2      The market was abuzz with talk that SingTel was only \par \par \uc2  halfway through meeting its dollar requirements for the deal. A \par \par \uc2  dealer at European bank said a local bank, believed to buying \par \par \uc2  on behalf of SingTel, had probably bought $2-$3 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The Sing dollar market is relatively small, and to meet \par \par \uc2  all the requirements for this deal at once will really upset \par \par \uc2  the market," said the dealer, adding that daily turnover in the \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was between $1-$2 billion. \par \par \uc2  Even though there has been scant sign of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore despite the Sing's rapid decline, \par \par \uc2  analysts said the authorities were unlikely to change their \par \par \uc2  policy stance of a gradually stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The MAS has always been very clear that they regard the \par \par \uc2  exchange rate as a tool to fight inflation, not as a way to \par \par \uc2  compete on exports," said Gerard Teo, regional economist at \par \par \uc2  ABN-AMRO in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He pointed out that while the Sing dollar has weakened \par \par \uc2  significantly, it was still within its trading band of its \par \par \uc2  trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  INDONESIA'S PARADE OF WOES \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was once again at the mercy of \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  volatile politics, though wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept it well behaved. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said the market was also reluctant to \par \par \uc2  push the dollar higher in case the Indonesian Bank \par \par \uc2  Restructuring Agency converted more of a total of $500 million \par \par \uc2  from recent asset sales. \par \par \uc2  However, the rupiah remained on the backfoot as President \par \par \uc2  Abdurrahman Wahid responded to a parliamentary censure of him \par \par \uc2  over two financial scandals. \par \par \uc2      Wahid apologised for any "inappropriate behaviour" but \par \par \uc2  remained steadfast in his rejection of the censure. \par \par \uc2      Fears of violence between Wahid's supporters and opponents \par \par \uc2  were brewing in Jakarta, threatening to roil the country's \par \par \uc2  already fragile markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0849 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.74\tab  122.67\tab    +0.76\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7927\t